\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  gain, peso and rupiah weaken on domestic concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2018\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Mixed signals in Indonesia on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  support hit rupiah\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  signals possible rate hike next week\par     * Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shrug off U.S-China trade war\par developments\par \par     By Nikhil Nainan\par     Sept 19 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged higher on\par Wednesday, shrugging off  another round of tit-for-tat exchanges\par in the U.S.-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade war, while suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported the rupee.\par     The Chinese yuan allayed initial weakness at the\par open to strengthen 0.1 percent to 6.852 per dollar as Premier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li\par Keqiang\f28 \uc2 \f2  assured markets China would not devalue the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par boost exports.\par     "It is a shot in the arm for yuan bulls," said Wei Liang\par Chang, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     This week saw China and the United States plunge deeper into\par a trade war, as Washington planned to levy new tariffs of 10\par percent on $200 billion of Chinese products next week, to which\par with China responded with tariffs on about $60 billion worth of\par U.S. goods, as previously planned, but at a lower tariff rate.\par \par     Indonesia's rupiah weakened 0.2 percent to 14,885 to\par the dollar, on mixed messages from the government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on whether exporters will be required to keep earnings\par onshore and convert them to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Mandating export conversion and retention of earnings\par onshore may be effective in stabilising the rupiah once they\par have taken effect," Mizuho's Chang said. \par     "However, foreign investors might also question whether\par other capital flow measures may be forthcoming if volatility\par picks up again." \par      The Philippine peso fell 0.1 percent against the\par dollar to 54.07, even though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has signalled a\par fourth rate hike this year, which could come as soon as its\par Sept. 27 Monetary Board meeting. \par     The Philippines has been hit by rising costs, with annual\par inflation hitting 6.4 percent in August, prompting \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangko\par Sentral ng Pilipinas\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BSP) Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nestor Espenilla\f28 \uc2 \f2  to declare\par bringing inflation back to the 2-4 percent target range his most\par urgent task.\par     "Escalating inflation has deepened concerns of whether\par overheating will persist. This suggest that the current account\par deficit may still widen, if BSP rate hikes are viewed to be\par behind the curve," Mizuho's Chang added. \par     Malaysia's ringgit was little changed at 4.142 to the\par dollar after news that inflation rose 0.2 percent in August, the\par slowest in 3-1/2 years and below the 0.4 percent median forecast\par in a Reuters poll.\par     Inflation has been mild since the new Mahathir government\par scrapped a goods and services tax in June.\par     \par     THAI BAHT \par The baht was a shade firmer at 32.55 per dollar, hours\par ahead of a key policy meeting where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely\par expecting to hold rates, although expectations of a rate hike\par before year-end have surfaced.\par     Both DBS and OCBC banks expect no change in rates, though\par OCBC expects \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to hike once by year-end as\par inflation edges closer to the mid-point of its 1-4 percent\par target.\par     "Unlike some of its emerging market peers, Thailand is not\par under pressure to raise rates to stabilise its exchange rate,"\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 DBS Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note. \par     \par     INDIAN RUPEE\par The rupee strengthened 0.5 percent to 72.595 as traders\par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar selling after it hit yet another\par record low on Tuesday.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fallen 12 percent so far this year and is\par the region's worst performer, prompting investors to wager that\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will need to raise rates at least twice more \par this year to shore up the battered rupee.\par     "A rate hike is necessary given the negative flow\par environment to stabilise sentiment, but its impact on the rupee\par may be discounted as long as oil prices keep rising," said\par Chang.\par         \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at 0510 GMT                          \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    112.330     112.35        +0.02\par  Sing dlr                     1.370       1.3706        +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.773      30.813        +0.13\par  Korean won                   1123.200    1123.2   