\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Faced with trade war risk, yuan to manage only modest rise\b0\par\par\uc2 805 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2018\par 02:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=CNY= poll data for Chinese yuan\par \par \uc2 By Vivek Mishra\par \par \uc2 BENGALURU, Sept 6 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan will trim only some of its recent losses against the dollar over the coming year, with the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasingly likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a still-rampant dollar, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 Trading in the partly-managed yuan, which has lost about 5 percent since the start of the year, was volatile this week amid threats that U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could impose additional tariffs on Chinese goods worth $200 billion.\par \par \uc2 But in the last few weeks, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and avoid heavy capital outflows, strengthening the yuan by about 1.5 percent against the greenback from its weakest level this year on August 15.\par \par \uc2 "Chinese authorities, having allowed the yuan to weaken in response to the trade escalation, have now signaled that they are unwilling to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide further beyond the 6.95\u8211\'20\'137.00 level last seen in late 2016," noted Khoon Goh, Head of Asia Research at ANZ.\par \par \uc2 "In the past, the authorities have been successful in eventually turning yuan weakness around. Trade tension is unresolved and the PBoC is likely to further support growth. But even with this, the signal the PBoC is sending suggests the yuan could be due for a rebound in the near-term."\par \par \uc2 The yuan is expected to gain 1 percent to 6.77 per dollar in a year, according to the poll of over 50 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists taken Sept 3-5 from around 6.84 late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 However, 18 of 40 common contributors have now revised their forecasts to a weaker yuan compared with a poll taken last month, citing the risk that global trade tensions worsen.\par \par \uc2 Thirteen of them kept their projections unchanged and the remaining 9 revised them to reflect a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nine strategists see the yuan weakening to 7 to the dollar or higher at some point over the 12-month period, two more than in the poll taken one month ago.\par \par \uc2 The PBoC has taken multiple steps to arrest the sharply-depreciating yuan by making the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expensive for investors to bet on, helping to ease market speculation in a bid to avoid a repeat of the shock devaluation of the renminbi seen in 2015.\par \par \uc2 One of the measures the PBoC undertook to shore up the yuan was to reintroduce the 'counter-cyclical factor' to its daily fixing mechanism at the end of August. This would allow investors to trade 2 percent above or below the daily reference rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following this, bearish bets on the renminbi were sharply reduced, a separate Reuters survey showed.\par \par \uc2 "We are fairly bearish on the U.S. dollar over the near-term and see weakness in the yuan as a multi-reflection of dollar strength," said Erik Nelson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  and the top forecaster for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2017.\par \par \uc2 "In the very near-term the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is out of the woods, but I think by early next year we will see a decisive recovery in the yuan and decisive resumption of greenback weakness."\par \par \uc2 But the wider Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll found the U.S. dollar, which has had its best run so far this year since 2015, will hold on to the gains until December and not beyond.\par \par \uc2 Still, the 12-month forecast for the yuan was the most pessimistic median in Reuters polls conducted this year.\par \par \uc2 Several \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said renewed pressure on the yuan is inevitable as the Sino-U.S. trade war escalates, threatening to put more pressure on China's already cooling economy.\par \par \uc2 Seventeen of 50 participants said the yuan will weaken below the current level of 6.84 in a year with the most pessimistic forecast expecting it to fall to 7.30, a level not seen since last financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Policy tightening from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  and rising Treasury yields could affect the yuan's stability.\par \par \uc2 "The prospect of a new trade war could hurt China's export competitiveness and the PBoC is loosening monetary policy to cope with credit contraction. So I don't deny for a moment that yuan will face depreciation pressure," said Li Yishuang, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 China Securities\uc2  in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 "The chance of yuan falling below 7 in the short-term is low, but in the long-term, the movement will depend on dollar index."\par \par \uc2 (Other stories from the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll: ) (Polling by Khushboo Mittal and Vivek Mishra Editing by Ross Finley and Matthew Mpoke Bigg)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-9T00:05:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180906ee960008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
