\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Timeline of China's recent measures to stabilise yuan amid trade tensions\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2018\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Sept 3 (Reuters) - \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rolled out a series of regulatory measures in recent weeks to arrest losses in the yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is facing depreciation pressures amid a worsening trade dispute with Washington and as Beijing seeks to boost slowing economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has fallen more than 6 percent against the U.S. dollar since mid-June.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the latest steps may have prevented an imminent test of the sensitive 7 yuan to the dollar level, last seen during the global financial crisis. But with U.S. tariffs set to escalate, more pressure is inevitable and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to decide soon whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more forcefully.\par \par \uc2 Following is a timeline of recent policy moves and official market-stabilising statements by the People's Bank of China (PBOC):\par \par \uc2 ** Aug 24 - The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  says it has adjusted its methodology for fixing the yuan's daily midpoint by re-introducing a "counter-cyclical factor" in order to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stable, amid broad dollar strength and trade tensions between Washington and Beijing.\par \par \uc2 ** Aug 16 - China bans commercial banks from using some interbank accounts to deposit or lend yuan offshore through free trade zone schemes, sources told Reuters, closing a loophole for potential capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 ** Aug 6 - \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is said to have urged some banks to prevent "herd behaviour" and momentum-chasing moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a Bloomberg report said, citing unnamed sources.\par \par \uc2 ** Aug 3 - The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  announced it is setting a reserve requirement ratio of 20 percent for financial institutions settling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward dollar sales to clients, effectively raising the cost for investors shorting the yuan. ** July 19 - \uc2 Wang Chunying\uc2 , spokeswoman at the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE), tells reporters the regulator would bolster "macro-prudential management" and "micro-level market supervision" and use "counter-cyclical" measures to deal with instability.\par \par \uc2 ** July 3 - PBOC Governor \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  says it is closely watching fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and would seek to keep the yuan at a stable and reasonable level.\par \par \uc2 ** Major state-owned Chinese banks have been seen swapping yuan for dollars in forwards since mid-June, traders said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the yuan's anticipated value against the dollar in a year's time sharply higher.\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Winni Zhou and Andrew Galbraith; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-3T04:48:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180903ee9300aq6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
