\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Turkey crisis rips through emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , sends stocks down 1.8%\b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2018\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Turkish lira hits record low of 7.24 to the dollar overnight\par \par \uc2 * Lira crisis hits South African rand, Russian rouble, China yuan\par \par \uc2 * MSCI EM stock index falls 1.8%, close to more than 1 year low\par \par \uc2 By Karin Strohecker and Swati Pandey\par \par \uc2 LONDON/SYDNEY, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The crisis engulfing Turkish markets over its diplomatic rift with the United States sent tremors through emerging markets on Monday, knocking some main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to multi-year lows and weighing heavily on equities.\par \par \uc2 Investors fear the selloff in the lira, which hit a fresh record low overnight, could have a ripple effect in global financial markets, with the euro, South Africa's rand and Mexico's peso already dented by Turkey's crisis.\par \par \uc2 The lira pared some of its losses against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had lowered reserve requirement ratios for banks as well as pledged to provide whatever liquidity banks needed and to take all necessary measures to maintain financial stability.\par \par \uc2 However, the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still down more than 6 percent on the day and within spitting distance of a record low around 7.24 hit it early Asian trade. The lira has weakened nearly 45 percent since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's local bond markets saw yields spike above 21 percent, while dollar-denominated bonds issued by the government and banks suffered a steep selloff. Istanbul's stock exchange halted trading in three of the country's leading banks after they tumbled more than 11 percent.\par \par \uc2 "It's a textbook crisis \u8211\'20\'13 for many years everybody said Turkey was a weak country due to its large external debt and current account deficit," said Guillaume Tresca, senior emerging markets strategist at Credit Agricole.\par \par \uc2 "There is nothing surprising other than that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not really reacting. They issued this new plan but there is no tightening of financial conditions \u8211\'20\'13 they are completely behind the curve."\par \par \uc2 Other main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were caught in the vortex. South Africa's rand skidded to levels not seen since mid-2016 and Russia's rouble slumped to a near 2-1/2 year trough.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee slid to an all-time trough, while the Indonesian rupiah hitting a near three-year low prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan weakened 0.5 percent - its steepest daily decline in nearly four weeks.\par \par \uc2 The wave of selling was triggered on Friday when U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced tougher sanctions on Turkish steel and aluminium exports, causing a spike in emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility gauges.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the emerging market woes, Washington imposed surprise sanctions last week against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Some safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds rallied. The dollar index held near its one-year top of 96.522, while the Japanese yen climbed for a second straight day to a 1-1/2 month peak.\par \par \uc2 However, the sell-off was not limited to emerging markets: the euro stumbled to more than one-year lows on worries about European bank exposure to Turkey.\par \par \uc2 Spain's \uc2 BBVA\uc2 , Italy's \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  and France's \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  have some of the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Turkey among the euro zone banks.\par \par \uc2 The fear of contagion reverberated across equity markets.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's broadest emerging markets index slipped 1.8 percent and traded within eyesight of a one-year low hit in June. The benchmark was pulled lower by hefty falls in Asian heavyweights South Korea and Hong Kong, where indexes fell around 1.5 percent, while Taiwan tumbled more than 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Swati Pandey in Sidney and Karin Strohecker in London, additional reporting by Claire Milhench in London, Editing by Gareth Jones) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-13T10:30:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180813ee8d01b81\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
