\par\par \b \uc2 Global Equities Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2018\par 10:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering Equities. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 0805 GMT - Shares in \uc2 Merck KGaA\uc2  lost as much as 3.8% as the company's Life Sciences division missed expectations due to unusual selling patterns--with more low-margin hardware sold this quarter--and a gene-editing investment, says Bryan Garnier. However, 2Q organic growth was slightly ahead. Healthcare did well but was affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  headwinds. Shares trade down 3.2% at EUR87.56. (donatopaolo.mancini@dowjones.com; @donatopmancini)\par \par \uc2 0759 GMT - Though just a 0.1 percentage-point increase by Hong Kong's 3 major lenders, the mortgage-rate increase has nonetheless resulted in developers falling slightly amid today's strong gains in the city's stock market. Earnings impact will be limited on both the builders and banks, says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  , but it says a bigger affect on sentiment will occur if the prime rate rises following next month's anticipated Fed hike. Hong Kong's prime rate has been steady since 2008 and is the main reference point for mortgage lending there. (john.wu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0754 GMT - \uc2 Deutsche Post\uc2  's management seems to have stabilized underperforming businesses, while profit momentum is building up in the forwarding division, according to \uc2 HSBC\uc2  . "Risks of further internally generated disappointment seem to have abated," the bank says, raising the stock to buy from hold. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says the company's second-quarter results came without surprises--"no more bad news is good news," it says--and that early indications point at price increases in the German parcel market sticking. With performance at the post, e-commerce, parcel division stabilized, the bank says it expects profits to recover in line with management's 2020 targets. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  raises the target price to EUR38.50 from EUR30.50. Shares are up 0.6% at EUR31.26. (alberto.delclaux@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0754 GMT - \uc2 Card Factory\uc2  's 1H like-for-like sales performance is disappointing, but given the tough retail environment it could have been worse, says \uc2 Liberum\uc2 . The retailer posted a 0.2% fall in 1H like-for-like sales compared with a 3.1% sales growth in the same period a year earlier, due to weak consumer environment and extreme weather. The brokerage says \uc2 Card Factory\uc2  's website had a strong performance, but its online gift business, Getting Personal, continues to be disappointing with sales down 8.5% due to tough competition and rising costs. \uc2 Card Factory\uc2  shares are down 7.4% to 195.20 pence.(maryam.cockar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0750 GMT - \uc2 L'Oreal\uc2  is downgraded to sell from hold by Berenberg, who says the French company's valuation offers little upside in the absence of cash deployment beyond bolt-on acquisitions. Despite this, Berenberg says \uc2 L'Oreal\uc2  's second-quarter results show that topline momentum is continuing, although it is unbalanced in terms of channels and divisions. "Luxury continues to be the main driver, boosted by strong Chinese consumption," Berenberg says, adding that it expects a normalization of trends in China, Hong Kong and Asia travel retail to hit \uc2 L'Oreal\uc2  's growth in 2019. \uc2 L'Oreal\uc2  shares trade down 0.9% at EUR210.60. (anthony.shevlin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0747 GMT - Asian stock markets were all over the map Thursday, with local factors dominating amid a lack of overseas trading cues. Potential government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in tech sent the sector higher in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fueling gains of more than 2% for major indexes. That also helped Hong Kong. A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped Japan's stocks while a weaker one helped fuel New Zealand's. Australia briefly hit another 10 1/2-year high on earnings news, but the Philippines fell 0.4%, well off session lows, after a weak GDP report and ahead of the imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy statement. The moves came as India's Sensex continued to hit more record highs. S&P 500 futures are flat. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 0728 GMT - The roller-coaster ride that's been Chinese stocks of late continued today, and it was a climb. As the major indexes logged gains nearly as big as Tuesday's pops, the Shanghai Composite rose 1.8% to 2794.38 and the Shenzhen Composite jumped 2.7%. The startup-heavy ChiNext did top Tuesday's gain in bouncing 3.4%. Techs led, with \uc2 ZTE\uc2  logging a 10% limit-up gain along with more than 20 hardware, chip and 5G names amid potential of government action. The badly battered health-care sector also rebounded while energy stocks retreated on oil's overnight slump. With earnings season looming, \uc2 Citic Securities\uc2  says banks will likely be the upcoming focus amid slower deleveraging efforts. (john.wu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Cheers,\par \par \uc2 John\par \par \uc2 0658 GMT - \uc2 Thyssenkrupp\uc2  's new long-term earnings and cash-flow targets aren't likely to persuade the market as long as short-term uncertainties remain, \uc2 Baader Bank\uc2  analyst Christian Obst says. The group published a target to hit EUR1 billion in free cash flow before mergers and acquisitions by its 2021 fiscal year alongside its third-quarter earnings. However, until the company finds a new CEO and supervisory board chairman, resolves the issues surrounding the proposed joint venture with \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  and finds a way to bolster earnings at its industrial solutions unit, the targets will remain a secondary concern, he says. (nathan.allen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0649 GMT - Nordic stock markets are seen opening just in positive territory Thursday with IG calling the OMXS30 up 0.1% at around 1624. "With another quiet day on the economic data front, the market will focus on geopolitical developments around Russia and Turkey, where the U.S. has adopted new sanctions," says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  . The U.S. equity markets were range bound yesterday and it is again a mixed picture for Asian equity markets this morning. "China is preparing to retaliate against the rise in U.S. tariffs, and has announced that it will impose tariffs of 25% on $16 billion of U.S. goods imported by China." OMXS30 closed at 1622.63, OMXN40 at 1545.29 and OBX at 839.25. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0648 GMT - \uc2 Zurich Insurance\uc2  's first-half net profit and operating profit came in above expectations, meaning there's a good chance of a healthy payout for shareholders, \uc2 Vontobel\uc2  says. "Zurich reports pleasing 1H 2018 results with solid progress on the non-life side and a good increase on the life-insurance side," it says. The Swiss insurance giant reported a 19% increase in net profit, which came in at $1.79 billion. Business operating profit also rose, standing at $2.42 billion compared with $2.17 billion a year earlier. "Zurich appears well on track to at least match last year's high dividend," \uc2 Vontobel\uc2  says. (pietro.lombardi@dowjones.com; @pietrolombard10)\par \par \uc2 0649 GMT - The global solar-energy market is maturing. Amid a curb on new approvals in China, the amount of solar-panel systems installed is set to fall 13% this year to 85 gigawatts of power production, predicts Tom Heggarty at \uc2 Wood Mackenzie\uc2 . A decline hasn't happened since 2000, he adds. Also capping the industry this year is a potential drop in India due to the recent imposition of import duties. China accounts for over half of the global solar market while India's market share is estimated to be around 9%. (biman.mukherji@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0648 GMT - Adidas's strong second-quarter results are above expectations and the company continues to outperform its U.S. peers, analysts at Baader Helvea say. Adidas's sales rose 10%, excluding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  effects. Baader says Adidas's 16% growth in North America compares favorably with recent updates from \uc2 Nike\uc2  and \uc2 Under Armour\uc2  . "After 1H18, we see Adidas ahead of its full-year targets," Baader says. (anthony.shevlin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 09, 2018 04:05 ET (08:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180809ee89001ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
