\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Dollar Retreats as Chinese, Japanese  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Gain\b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Kruger \par \uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2018\par 19:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell Tuesday after China showed signs it is supporting the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of 16 others, declined 0.3% to 88.73. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday had reached its highest level since May 2017.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against China's yuan as traders at four major financial institutions in Shanghai said the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shifted away from traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or selling billions of dollars to buy yuan, instead acting through lower-profile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps.\par \par \uc2 The policy has helped boost China's stockpile of foreign reserves. Those reserves rose slightly to about $3.12 trillion last month from $3.11 trillion in June -- a second consecutive month of increases. That stability helps bolster confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , amid concerns that the strong U.S. dollar could encourage the flow of capital out of China.\par \par \uc2 Analysts and investors have been concerned that rapid declines in the yuan could suggest large capital outflows, or determine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to prop it up.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell after Reuters reported that officials with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  had considered raising interest rates earlier in the year, and are looking for ways to step back from years of easy-money policies that helped lead to the country's adoption of negative interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The report "suggests the path of policy going forward is less, not more, easy," said \uc2 Mazen Issa\uc2 , a strategist at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Write to Daniel Kruger at Daniel.Kruger@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 07, 2018 13:38 ET (17:38 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180807ee87002zl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
