\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: Stocks Jump on Banking Gains, Data\b0\par\par\uc2 1,451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2018\par 12:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Markets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks jumped Tuesday, as gains for \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and other banks helped push the market toward its first advance in four sessions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Equities held to higher ground after preliminary manufacturing activity data for the eurozone in July came in above expectations.\par \par \uc2 "After a quiet start, the equity bulls have come charging into the fray, emboldened by \uc2 Google\uc2  's figures, China's move towards infrastructure stimulus and a decent set of PMIs from the eurozone, with Germany's manufacturing \uc2 PMI\uc2  in particular receiving plenty of garlands," said Chris Beauchamp at spread-betting firm IG.\par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 index added 0.9% to reach 388.51, topped by the basic materials and financial groups. But the oil and gas, utility and health care sectors lost ground.\par \par \uc2 Germany's DAX 30 index claimed a 1.4% rise, France's CAC 40 picked up 1% and Italy's FTSE MIB jumped 1.2%. Spain's IBEX 35 gained 0.9% and the U.K.'s FTSE 100 index was 0.8% higher.\par \par \uc2 Broad gains for lenders pulled the Stoxx Europe 600 Banks Index up by 1.8%, on track for its largest gain in six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Shares of constituent \uc2 UBS\uc2  climbed more than 3%, shaping up for its largest advance since early June. In its second-quarter earnings report, the Swiss lender's profit topped expectations, boosted by the performance of its investment-bank businesses.\par \par \uc2 A promise of new stimulus out of China was being assessed by investors. \uc2 China's State Council\uc2  outlined measures aimed at bolstering domestic consumption, such as corporate tax cuts and support for small businesses. Bond yields rose in China on the news, a day after U.S. Treasurys and other sovereign bonds gained on reports that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  may discuss tweaking its yield curve control policy. Rising bond yields can provide a boost to lenders.\par \par \uc2 European stocks remained higher after the first reading of manufacturing data in the eurozone for July surpassed expectations. The data arrived before Thursday's meeting of \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy makers.\par \par \uc2 "Surging government bond yields (U.S., Japan), supported by [Federal Reserve ] monetary policy tightening and \uc2 BOJ\uc2  tweaking are boosting Banks & Financials, while expectations of an upcoming meeting between U.S. President Trump and \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President Juncker is smoothing some of the trade war concerns," said analysts at \uc2 Accendo Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That said, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains under pressure, forcing Beijing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday," they added in a note.\par \par \uc2 Stocks in focus:\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  rose 3.4% as the Swiss bank said second-quarter net profit increased by 9.4% to 1.28 billion Swiss francs ($1.29 billion), and analysts had expected net profit of CHF1.02 billion.\par \par \uc2 Peugeot\uc2  shares soared 11% as the French auto maker's first-half profit came in at 1.48 billion euros ($1.73 billion), above expectations of EUR1.15 billion.\par \par \uc2 Randstad\uc2  moved up by 5% after the Dutch recruitment company said adjusted net profit-excluding amortization, impairments and one-off costs- rose 23% to EUR223 million in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 Economic data:\par \par \uc2 In July, the manufacturing purchasing managers' index beat expectations, printing 55.1, \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2  reported Tuesday. That compares with the 54.7 expectation from a \uc2 FactSet\uc2  consensus survey. The services \uc2 PMI\uc2  of 54.4, however, fell short of the 55.0 estimate.\par \par \uc2 French and German manufacturing PMIs for July also exceeded expectations. On the services side, German activity was in line with estimates, but the French services \uc2 PMI\uc2  fell slightly short.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, confidence in French manufacturing dropped in July, with business leaders less optimistic about activity in the sector for the coming months than they had been earlier this year, French \uc2 statistics agency Insee\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The sentiment reading in the manufacturing sector declined to 108 in July from 109 in June, which \uc2 Insee\uc2  revised down from a previous reading of 110.\par \par \uc2 In commodities, Brent crude oil gained just 5 cents to $73.12 a barrel. Gold edged down 0.1% to $1,233.15 an ounce. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par American Markets Outlook: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks were poised for modest gains Tuesday as the prospect of Chinese stimulus lifted European and Asian markets and investors put their concerns over trade frictions on hold.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures for the Dow Industrials and S&P 500 were up 0.1% ahead of the open. Yields on 10-year Treasurys declined slightly to 2.959% from 2.963% Monday. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar held steady in Asia after regaining some strength Monday, with the WSJ Dollar index up 0.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro traded at $1.1690, barely moving from $1.1694 late Monday in New York. The dollar continued to rise against the yuan, climbing 0.3% to 6.814. That puts the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at its weakest level in just over a year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite this, there is little indication that China is weakening the yuan to retaliate against U.S. tariffs, according to Paul Kitney, chief equity strategist at Daiwa Capital Markets. He said local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Australia, India, the Philippines and South Korea had all fallen further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In turn, that implies Chinese companies and individuals aren't rushing to sell yuan, Mr. Kitney said. "Unlike 2016, when the Chinese authorities were fighting hard against gaps in the capital account and associated rising credit risks, the present situation does not demonstrate such capital flight," he said in a note. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Top Stories: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone Business Activity Slips\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurozone business activity slipped in July after a brief rebound in June, as the economy struggles to gain momentum following a soft start to 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Peugeot\f28 \uc2 \f2  First-Half Profit Rises\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Peugeot\f28 \uc2 \f2  said an improved performance at its core automotive division helped lift first-half net profit to \u8364\'20\'AC1.48 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  Profit Boosted by Investment Banking\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  said strong gains at its investment bank boosted overall profit in the last quarter, but warned political and trade tensions could shake investor confidence in financial markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Analysis: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EU Counts on Top Official to Try to Calm U.S. Trade Fight\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EU is cautiously betting on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jean-Claude Juncker\f28 \uc2 \f2  , its unconventional top official, to persuade President Trump not to escalate the trans-Atlantic trade fight.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sergio Marchionne\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Exit Jolts Ferrari\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sergio Marchionne\f28 \uc2 \f2  's exit as the leader of Ferrari is likely to upend an Italian sports-car legend whose strategy he revolutionized-including a production ramp-up, an IPO and the planned launch of an SUV. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Other News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French July Business Sentiment Falls to 108 From 109 in June\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Confidence in French manufacturing dropped in July, with business leaders less optimistic about activity in the sector for the coming months than they had been earlier this year, French \f28 \uc2 \f2 statistics agency Insee\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greek Wildfires Devastate Resort Area Near Athens\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uncontrolled wildfires intensified near Athens, killing at least 49 people and injuring dozens more as gale-force winds raged through holiday resorts in Greece's deadliest fire season in more than a decade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Randstad\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q Net Profit Rises 27%, Organic Revenue Growth Slows\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Randstad NV\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RAND.AE) said Tuesday that net profit jumped 27% in the second quarter on organic revenue growth that slowed from the previous quarter to 5%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Global News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fund Managers See Caution Signs in Emerging-Market Bond Rebound\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging-market government bonds have bounced back from their decline in the first half of 2018, but many bond-fund managers aren't buying the rebound.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Ad Business Boosts Earnings, Offsets Android Fine\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alphabet\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported sales and profit surpassing analysts' estimates, a sign that its strength in online ads will help offset the impact of European regulations for online privacy and perceived abuses of its position in the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trump and Iran Leader Swap Taunts as Sanctions Loom\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Trump administration exchanged threats with Iran, turning to a longstanding security concern and a top foreign-policy focus of President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  's key supporters. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ================================= \par Still To Come: \par Tuesday, July 24, 2018 \par GMT                   Exp    Prev \par 1145 US      Retail Economist/ \par              \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2   Weekly \par              Chain Store Sales \par              W/W%           -0.5% \par              M/M%           +4.0% \par 1230 US  Q1  GDP by State \par 1255 US      Johnson Redbook \par              Retail Sales Index \par              M/M%           +0.1% \par              Y/Y%           +3.3% \par              Latest Wk, Y/Y% \par                             +3.3% \par 1300 US  May House Price Index \par 1345 US  Jul Flash Services PMI \par                              56.5 \par 1345 US  Jul Flash Manufacturing \par              PMI             54.6 \par 1400 US  Jul \f28 \uc2 \f2 Richmond Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par              Business Activity \par              Survey            20 \par              Shipments         17 \par 2030 US      API Weekly \par              Statistical Bulletin \par              Crude          +0.6M \par              Gasoline       +0.4M \par              Distillate     +1.7M \par 2301 UK Jul  REC JobsOutlook \par              survey \par ================================= \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to paul.larkins@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 24, 2018 06:06 ET (10:06 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180724ee7o000xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
