\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-China's yuan to remain pressured by trade spat with U.S.\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2018\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=CNY= poll data\par \par \uc2 By Jonathan Cable\par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 6 (Reuters) - China's yuan will have failed to reverse June's losses against the U.S. dollar even in a year from now, according to a Reuters poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists that was conducted before the U.S. was due to impose steep tariffs on Chinese exports.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been volatile in the run-up to the U.S. levying tariffs on Chinese goods. It had its worst month on record in June, losing about 3.3 percent of its value against the greenback, and the slide continued into July.\par \par \uc2 At the start of the week, the yuan, which is closely managed by the Chinese authorities, fell as far as 6.72 per dollar, weaker than the most pessimistic one-month forecast of 6.60 in the last monthly Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 "Risks for a softer yuan have increased recently given the rising threat of larger tariffs being imposed by the U.S. on China," said Edoardo Campanella at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the yuan rebounded on Tuesday after People's Bank of China Governor \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would seek to keep the yuan at a stable and reasonable level. It continued to ride the updraft on Wednesday but struggled on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The yuan was trading around 6.64 per dollar on Thursday and will be around the same level in a month. At year-end, the yuan will have strengthened to 6.57 and then go stronger to 6.50 in a year, the poll of over 60 strategists taken this week showed.\par \par \uc2 Those median forecasts were weaker than in a June poll and the most pessimistic 12-month forecast moved from 6.80 to 7.20 per dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has previously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yuan, triggering accusations that Beijing was trying to gain an unfair competitive advantage for its exporters - charges revived by U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. president has said tariffs would make the U.S. stronger and levies on $34 billion worth of Chinese exports will kick in later on Friday. Beijing has said it would retaliate with tariffs on U.S. products.\par \par \uc2 But Trump has threatened to escalate the trade conflict with tariffs on as much as $400 billion in Chinese goods if Beijing does retaliate.\par \par \uc2 "A very tricky period lies ahead for China. Growth is under pressure; exports are under pressure; stocks are under pressure; and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure," said Michael Every at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . "Warning shots all round, in fact."\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the Reuters global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll: )\par \par \uc2 (Polling by Khushboo Mittal and Anisha Sheth; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-6T04:10:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180706ee76004v6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
