\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-WRAPUP 4-China's yuan gains on \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's calming words, stock markets unconvinced\b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2018\par 10:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional codes. No change to text.)\par \par \uc2 * Markets await U.S. trade tariff deadline this week\par \par \uc2 * Yuan likely to consolidate at current level - trader\par \par \uc2 * Stocks remain under pressure\par \par \uc2 By Winni Zhou and John Ruwitch\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, July 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose sharply against the dollar on Wednesday, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assured markets it would keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable amid heightened worries about trade frictions, although stocks fell.\par \par \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equity markets have been volatile ahead of July 6, when U.S. tariffs on $34 billion worth of Chinese goods are set to kick in. Beijing has said it would retaliate with tariffs on U.S. products.\par \par \uc2 The yuan had its worst month on record in June, losing about 3.3 percent of its value against the greenback, and the slide continued on Monday, the first trading day of July.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, though, it rebounded after the remarks from People's Bank of China Governor \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  and continued to ride the updraft on Wednesday, putting the yuan on track for its first two-day winning streak since the middle of June and best day since late March.\par \par \uc2 At 0800 GMT, it was trading at 6.6126 yuan per dollar, about 0.5 percent stronger than the late night close on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Thankfully for regional risk, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  engaged the yuan airbrake yesterday afternoon and at least for the time being, with the help of Chinese state-owned banks who were seen selling dollars to prop up the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is restoring a sense of calm in regional markets," \uc2 OANDA\uc2  wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 A trader at a Chinese bank said the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's signal was clear, but the market would closely watch developments ahead of Friday.\par \par \uc2 "In the short term, the yuan will continue consolidating at the current level, while sharp, one-way falling might have come to an end," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 Despite the market tumult earlier this week, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears broadly comfortable with a weakening yuan and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to prevent any destabilising declines or to restore market confidence, policy insiders told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Authorities are also confident they won't have to make heavy use of the official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the yuan as they did during 2015 when stocks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  went into a tailspin.\par \par \uc2 However, key Chinese equity indexes were not so re-assured, starting the day flip-flopping around Tuesday's closing prices before sliding into negative territory and staying there.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark CSI300 Index ended the day down 1.3 percent, and the Shanghai Composite Index was off 0.94 percent.\par \par \uc2 A person with knowledge of the plan told Reuters that Chinese tariffs on $34 billion of U.S. goods would take effect from midnight Beijing time on July 6 in response to the U.S. move.\par \par \uc2 In flagging its first move, Washington said it would implement its tariffs on July 6, but the 12-hour time difference technically puts Beijing ahead in imposing its reciprocal measures.\par \par \uc2 Also muddying trade relations between the world's two largest economies was a Chinese court ruling that temporarily barred U.S. chipmaker \uc2 Micron Technology Inc\uc2  from selling some of its main products in the world's biggest memory chip market.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, whose economy is heavily reliant on global trade, warned risks to the global growth outlook have significantly increased due to the intensifying trade row between Washington and Beijing.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are quite pessimistic at this point, and the downward correction for traditional blue-chips, represented by the heavyweight 'nifty 50' firms, is not over yet," said Wang Mingli, an analyst with \uc2 Guoyuan Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An index tracking the 50 most representative blue-chips in Shanghai, dubbed China\u8217\'20\'19s "nifty 50", slid around 1 percent to a near 14-month low.\par \par \uc2 However, Wang saw investment value in some growth and tech firms, saying the authorities were attaching more importance to the country's tech sector amid a bitter trade spat with the United States.\par \par \uc2 In Hong Kong, the Hang Seng Index closed down 1 percent, while an index that tracks mainland companies had fallen about 1.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Caution will prevail" ahead of July 6, said Steven Leung, an analyst with UOB Kay Hian. (Additional reporting by Liu Luoyan Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-4T09:26:26.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180704ee7400at0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
