\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE- \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  to be less  \highlight22\uc2 interventionist \highlight\uc2  on yuan than in 2015 - sources\b0\par\par\uc2 972 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2018\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers seen comfortable with weaker yuan as economy slows\par \par \uc2 * But could step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fend off sharp slide\par \par \uc2 * Counter-cyclical factor, tighter curbs on fund outflows seen likely options\par \par \uc2 * Lesson learned from 2015: avoid heavy use of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, July 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is comfortable with a weakening yuan, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to prevent any rapid and destabilising declines or to restore market confidence, as the economy loses momentum and faces further risks from a heated trade dispute with the United States, policy insiders said.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, as stocks sank and the yuan fell through a key psychological level of 6.7 on the dollar, traders said state-owned banks, which sometimes act on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , made efforts to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All the same, authorities are confident they won't have to make heavy use of the official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the yuan like in 2015 when stocks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  went into a tail spin as capital outflows accelerated, three sources who are familiar with policymakers' thinking told Reuters before the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the lessons of 2015, Beijing considers it has the policies in place to prevent any destabilising sell-off in the yuan, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  underscored Beijing's desire to inject confidence in markets that have been roiled by the trade war fears, the sources say policymakers would tolerate a weaker yuan to help cushion a slowing economy and take some of the sting out of Washington's proposed tariffs on its exports to the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolicymakers believe some yuan depreciation is okay, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see it falling below 6.9. Appropriate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation is needed given that the economy faces downward pressure," one policy insider said.\par \par \uc2 A second policy source echoed those views: \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no big problem with the yuan depreciation. It could be beneficial as the economy is slowing. We are able to control capital outflows. There is no need for aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has yet to respond to Reuters' request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The yuan saw its worst month on record in June, falling about 3.3 percent against the dollar, drawing comparisons with the 2015 episode of sharp yuan depreciation which forced the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 to spend more than $800 billion to slow it down. The yuan bounced sharply on Wednesday, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  soothed nervous markets.\par \par \uc2 According to the policy insiders, it is unlikely \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced into large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Worries of destabilising outflows are being partly offset by the capital controls China has introduced to arrest the previous slide in the yuan and restore confidence in its financial assets.\par \par \uc2 The sources are involved in internal policy discussions but are not part of the final decision-making process. They spoke on condition on anonymity.\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY BETTER EQUIPPED\par \par \uc2 Besides the capital outflow risks, a sharp weakening in the yuan may pose financing problems for companies exposed to dollar-denominated debt.\par \par \uc2 Beijing is also expected to make use of other tools it has finessed since 2015, such as the "counter-cyclical factor" it introduced in May last year to the formula it uses to determine the mid-point reference rate for the yuan\u8217\'20\'19s exchange rate against the dollar each day. That factor was designed to curb speculation and volatility in the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities have become more experienced in managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a third source who advises the government. He expects some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 6.7-6.8 area.\par \par \uc2 "Currently, the pressure is not as big as in 2015 \u8230\'20\'26 if the depreciation trend continues like this, they could take some measures, including reviving the counter-cyclical factor, rather than heavy spending of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves."\par \par \uc2 Also, a years-long government-led crackdown on financial risks has meant China is better equipped to handle market ructions than in 2015 when the turmoil in stocks and the yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was partly blamed on bungled rescue attempts by the authorities.\par \par \uc2 Most measures taken since late 2015 to tighten controls on money moving out of the country, including closer scrutiny of outbound investments, large overseas money transfers and individual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases remain in place.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, China eased the tap a bit by granting qualified domestic financial institutions fresh quotas to buy overseas stocks and bonds, but the yuan depreciation has not come on the back of heavy outflows like two years ago.\par \par \uc2 "They can reintroduce the counter-cyclical factor, they can tighten capital controls, in the end they can even use a small amount of their reserves \u8230\'20\'26 but this time is different because there is already a strict regulation on capital outflows," said Mahamoud Islam, Hong Kong-based senior APAC economist at \uc2 Euler Hermes\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NO DELIBERATE YUAN-WEAKENING\par \par \uc2 Some policy advisers said authorities are also likely to use subtle measures, such as higher-than-expected midpoint yuan fixings to sound discomfort with the pace or direction of the moves and limit any large-scale direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The message that the recent yuan weakening is not deliberately driven by China resonates with many economists and investors and Tuesday's market action reinforced it.\par \par \uc2 "I don't believe they are using the yuan as a tool in negotiations with the U.S.," said Jean-Charles Sambor, deputy head of emerging market debt at \uc2 BNP Paribas Asset Management\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "They are less \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  than in the past, but I do think around 6.7 they may be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep confidence in the yuan and make sure they are not facing massive outflows."\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting and Writing by Marius Zaharia Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-4T08:40:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180704ee74009vo\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 RTTN\par \b \uc2 Sensex, Nifty Seen Flat To Lower\b0\par\par\uc2 editorial@rttnews.com (RTT Staff Writer) \par \uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2018\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018 RTTNews. All rights reserved \par \par \uc2 Indian shares may open flat to slightly lower on Wednesday as trade concerns lingered and oil prices climbed amid signs of a tightening U.S. market and the ongoing crude supply outage at \uc2 Syncrude Canada\uc2  in Alberta.Benchmark indexes Sensex and the Nifty finished modestly higher on Tuesday while the rupee ended up by 0.32 percent at 68.58 per dollar amid suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by RBI.There is no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupee is still overvalued by 5-7 percent in terms of real effective exchange rate, Niti Aayog vice-chairman Rajiv Kumar said on Tuesday.Asian stocks recouped some early losses as China's markets opened with an advance in the yuan, helped by verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 .The dollar edged down against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and oil traded above $74 a barrel while gold prices hit one-week high on dollar weakness.Overnight, U.S.\par \par \uc2  stocks fell ahead of the July 4th holiday and the July 6 deadline for the Trump Administration's planned imposition of tariffs on Chinese imports.The Dow and the S&P 500 dropped around half a percent, while the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite shed 0.9 percent.European markets ended Tuesday's session with strong gains after German Chancellor \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2  and her coalition partners reached a compromise deal on migration.The pan-European Stoxx Europe 600 index climbed 0.8 percent. The German DAX rose 0.9 percent, France's CAC 40 index gained 0.8 percent and the U.K.'s FTSE 100 added 0.6 percent.\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020180704ee740008m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
