\par\par \b \uc2 China's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Makes Round Trip as Trade War, Growth Concerns Whipsaw Market -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Varada Bhat \par \uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2018\par 18:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The yuan tumbled overnight amid trade tensions with the US, before \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm jittery investors.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit to an eleventh month low today after it fell nearly 1% against the US dollar in early trading, and recovered to gain 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 Win Thin, global head of emerging-markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, \uc2 BBH\uc2  said the recent weakness had sparked a lot of attention, but the drop reflects a general weakness in the emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After being one of the outperforming \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for most of the year, the yuan has become one of the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Asian markets. The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 3.6% in the past one month while two months ago it was up 3.2%.\par \par \uc2 "Despite these losses, it is still one of the performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year," Thin says. However, he believes it could depreciate another 2%, to 6.8 through mid-2019.\par \par \uc2 the yuan bounced today after \uc2 China \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  pledgedto "maintain the basic stability of yuan's exchange rate at a reasonable and balanced level." He attributed the decline to the strength of US dollar, external uncertainty, and some procyclical behaviors. He assured that China's fundamental were good and cross-border capital flows were generally balanced. He also said that the yuan wouldn't be used as a weapon in a trade war with the U.S.\par \par \uc2 A slowing economy and fear of escalating trade tensions have been weighing on Chinese markets as both countries are set to impose tariffs from Friday. Last week, the Shanghai Composite index slipped into the bear territory and trading near its lowest level in more than two years. Today, the benchmark index dropped more than 1% and rebounded later, closing up 0.4%.\par \par \uc2 Sign up to Review & Preview, a new daily email from Barron's. Every evening we'll review the news that moved markets during the day and look ahead to what it means for your portfolio in the morning. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Focus on Funds blog,  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.barrons.com/focus-on-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.barrons.com/focus-on-funds }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 03, 2018 12:52 ET (16:52 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180703ee7300293\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
