\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 4-China's shares, yuan roiled as U.S. tariff deadline looms\b0\par\par\uc2 917 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2018\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Downward trend continues after bounce on Friday\par \par \uc2 * Analyst says stock market could take months to bottom out\par \par \uc2 * ING, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  lower yuan forecasts\par \par \uc2 By Luoyan Liu and John Ruwitch\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, July 2 (Reuters) - Chinese stocks took a battering on Monday in an ominous start to July, days before U.S. tariffs on Chinese exports are due to take effect, with the Shanghai bourse hitting over two-year lows and the yuan falling amid worries the trade row could put the economy on the skids.\par \par \uc2 Investors are jittery ahead of a July 6 deadline when the United States is set to impose tariffs on $34 billion worth of goods from China, the epicentre of a heated trade dispute between Washington and major economies that has convulsed financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Beijing is expected to respond with tariffs of its own on U.S. goods as the trade fight between the world two biggest economies threatens to damage global trade and investment.\par \par \uc2 There was little relief for investors in Chinese assets as, even before the tariffs kick in, a private survey showed manufacturing activity in the world's second-largest economy slowed slightly.\par \par \uc2 "Expectations for the country's economic growth have worsened a lot, as investors worry that external risks will increase in the second half of the year," said Zhu Xiaochun, an analyst with Lianxun Securities.\par \par \uc2 The yuan, fresh off its worst month on record, lost more ground against the dollar, trading at around 6.6549 at 0738 GMT from a close of 6.6225 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the equity markets, the blue chip CSI300 index fell 2.93 percent, while the Shanghai Composite Index shed 2.52 percent to close at 2775.77 points - its lowest level since March 1, 2016.\par \par \uc2 The fall erased Friday's gains which came on the last trading day of a turbulent month, when markets bounced in one of their best days since mid-2016.\par \par \uc2 Just before the markets opened, a private Caixin/Markit manufacturing survey showed factory growth in China cooled a touch in June, yet more worrisome was a contraction in new export orders for the third straight month and the most in two years.\par \par \uc2 The exports data provided a sobering reminder of the potential fallout of the intensifying Sino-U.S. trade dispute, which investors fear will ripple through global supply chains in a blow to world growth.\par \par \uc2 Zhu said price/earnings ratios for banks, steelmakers and coal miners were low by historical standards, but general concern over the health of the economy was keeping investors on the sidelines.\par \par \uc2 Chen Xiaopeng, an analyst with Sealand Securities, said that bodes ill for investors in Chinese stocks.\par \par \uc2 "It could take at least several months for the major stock indexes to bottom out."\par \par \uc2 Uncertainties will reinforce investors' inclination to "huddle together for warmth" in outperforming sectors such as consumers and healthcare, Chen said.\par \par \uc2 An index tracking healthcare firms is up nearly 20 percent so far this year, while the Shanghai index is down around 15 percent.\par \par \uc2 DISMAL JUNE\par \par \uc2 June represented the worst month for Chinese stocks in more than two years and the yuan's biggest monthly fall on record.\par \par \uc2 The yuan fell more than 3 percent against the dollar in June and continued its slide despite a firmer-than-expected midpoint set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Investors don't care and spot yuan rates continued weakening," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 If the yuan's decline intensifies, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  economists wrote in a note on Monday that the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC)\uc2 , may step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "CNY may overshoot with shifting market expectations of policy stance amid higher trade tensions, but we don't expect policymakers to encourage material RMB depreciation. The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  could step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if depreciation risk intensifies," they wrote.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the last trading day of the month, ING lowered its yuan forecast to 7 per dollar by the end of the year from a previous forecast of 6.6, citing risks to the policy outlook.\par \par \uc2 "A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would, at most, be a shield, safeguarding wider damage from a trade war and the hurdles faced by Chinese companies' operating in the U.S.," it said. ING added it did not see any panic in the market.\par \par \uc2 ING's shift follows a similar move on June 24 by \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , which said it expected the yuan to depreciate to 6.8 per dollar by the end of this year and 7.2 by the end of 2019. It had previously forecast 6.4 yuan per dollar in each year.\par \par \uc2 The depreciation will be "driven by an important change of policy stance from tightening to loosening", it said.\par \par \uc2 Chinese 10-year treasury futures for September dipped in the morning but reversed course in the afternoon to inch up about 0.13 percent.\par \par \uc2 After rising last week to a more than one-year high on trade war fears, the cost to insure exposure to Chinese debt fell on Monday. The spread of the five-year credit default swap rate on Chinese sovereign debt fell 4.7 percent to 69.79 basis points.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's markets were closed on Monday for a public holiday to mark the 21st anniversary of the former British colony's return to Chinese rule. (Additional reporting by Winni Zhou and Andrew Galbraith; Editing by Sam Holmes, Jacqueline Wong & Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-2T10:32:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180702ee7200bdb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
