\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2018\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Stocks Drop as Trade Worries Persist \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lingering concerns about trade kept global stocks muted although gains in oil prices boosted shares of oil-and-gas companies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Warns of Growing Risks to Global Debt Markets \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  sounded an alarm over global debt markets, saying it sees pockets of risk to the stability of the financial system in places ranging from U.S. corporate borrowing to risky loans in Britain to foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lending to emerging markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Fed's Latest Challenge: Keeping Benchmark Rate in Check \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve recently tweaked how it sets short-term interest rates in an effort to keep them from drifting too high-but an increase in its benchmark raises questions about its ability to keep borrowing costs in check. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Trump Signals Easing of Demand for Tools to Limit Chinese Investment \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Trump suggested he will ease off his demands for new restrictions on Chinese investment in technology industries, relying instead on a 1988 law being updated by Congress that authorizes the government to review foreign investments for national-security problems. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Eurozone Bank Lending Picks Up \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recovery in eurozone bank lending continued in May, a trend which should underpin corporate investments in the region. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's 'Big Mama' Steps In as Yuan Tumbles Further \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yuan's decline, after it had earlier set the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at a six-month low against the U.S. dollar. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Rises as U.S. Threatens Iranian Oil Customers \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude prices continued to climb as traders mulled the potential threat to supply after the Trump administration raised pressure on Iran's oil industry. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par When China, U.S. Fight Over Trade, European Stocks Get Hurt \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's main stock benchmark entered bear-market territory as trade tensions continued to reverberate and investors grew more concerned about the world's second-largest economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par As Treasury Targets Workarounds to Tax Law, Impact May Extend Far \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury's attempt to curb efforts by high-tax states to work around deduction caps in the new U.S. tax law could also hit programs like the one that helps to fund a rural Georgia hospital. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Tariff Talk Has Slammed the IPO Window Shut for Car Makers \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Luxury car makers are in the eye of the trade storm unleashed by U.S. President Donald Trump . One consequence: Hoped-for IPOs of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aston Martin\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volvo Cars\f28 \uc2 \f2  and possibly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jaguar Land Rover\f28 \uc2 \f2  are looking unlikely, even though most brands are reporting record sales.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 27, 2018 07:00 ET (11:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180627ee6r00116\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\