\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-India's rupee to rebound but path rife with pitfalls\b0\par\par\uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2018\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=INR= INR poll data\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=CNY= CNY poll data\par \par \uc2 By Vivek Mishra\par \par \uc2 BENGALURU, June 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee will erase some of this year's losses against the dollar over the coming 12 months but high volatility in the run up to general elections in 2019 could send it off-piste, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 A selloff in emerging markets and a widening fiscal deficit, exacerbated by rising oil prices - India's biggest import bill - has hurt the rupee this year.\par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an 18-month low of 68.47 per dollar in May and is down over 5 percent so far this year, making it one of the worst performers in Asia.\par \par \uc2 But the rupee is forecast to rebound and gain slightly to 66.87 in a year from about 67.45 on Tuesday, according to the poll of about 30 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts taken after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  hiked interest rates on June 6.\par \par \uc2 That median, although slightly weaker than in May, was driven by expectations for Asia's third largest economy to remain the fastest growing major economy as it did in the first three months of 2018 and on predictions for further interest rate hikes from the RBI.\par \par \uc2 "The INR continues to be alluring with more robust growth and compelling \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve backstop," said Vishnu Varathan, head of economics and strategy for \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "So once election risks fade and oil price ascendancy is subdued by supply-demand gaps ironing out - mostly via higher U.S. and \uc2 OPEC\uc2  supply - we expect the rupee will regain some traction as some of the risk premium - which pressures the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  now - erodes."\par \par \uc2 The rupee was also expected to get a boost from a weaker dollar outlook.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the dollar to start weakening around the end of this year or the start of next year. Weaker dollar is expected to support most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Amy Yuan Zhuang, chief Asia analyst at Nordea.\par \par \uc2 But not everyone was convinced, with the year-ahead forecasts in the widest range in Reuters polls since July 2016, suggesting the rupee's level in the run up to the general elections next year is far from clear.\par \par \uc2 Rising inflation is a well-established risk and any further rapid rise in global crude prices would weigh heavily on the fiscal arithmetic, which is already widening.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the government is set to increase spending on populist measures ahead of the May general elections, which is likely to make foreign investors nervous.\par \par \uc2 Over a quarter of nearly 30 respondents in the latest poll, who gave a forecast for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a year, expect the rupee to weaken to below the historic low of 68.8985 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Indian rupee will depreciate particularly due to political uncertainties built-up before the general elections next year," according to Nirmal Bang's economist, Teresa John, who forecasts the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken to 70 in a year.\par \par \uc2 "Anything beyond the 70 mark should really be a cause for alarm, and if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls below 69.5, there will be heavy RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," John added.\par \par \uc2 STEADY YUAN TO GAIN SLIGHTLY\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan, which has gained nearly 1.6 percent so far in 2018, is expected to strengthen further to 6.38 per dollar in a year.\par \par \uc2 The standard deviation for yuan estimates, a commonly used gauge of dispersion, fell to the lowest since a poll in September 2016, suggesting \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep a tight leash on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amidst the U.S.-China trade spat.\par \par \uc2 But the yuan moves in the year ahead were expected to be largely dependent on how the dollar performs.\par \par \uc2 A similar poll last week predicted the U.S. dollar's dominance will fade soon, with any sudden change in expectations for the policies of central banks posing the biggest risk.\par \par \uc2 "The era of a strong dollar is close to the end. Although the recent upward momentum in the U.S. dollar may continue in the short-term, the dollar will remain week in the long-run as the \uc2 ECB\uc2  and the BOJ tighten their monetary policy," said Li Yishuang, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 China Securities\uc2  in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 "So, we expect the yuan will strengthen slightly over the next 12 months."\par \par \uc2 For other stories from Reuters' global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll, see (Polling by Khushboo Mittal and Shaloo Shrivastava; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-6-13T04:20:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180613ee6d006v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
