\par\par \b \uc2 HK Bourse: Results Announcement From \uc2 Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd\uc2  .\b0\par\par\uc2 12,182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 12:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     For full details, please click on the following link: \par  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2018/0327/LTN20180327703.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2018/0327/LTN20180327703.pdf }}}\uc2 \f2  \par  \par  \par  \par                       ANNOUNCEMENT OF RESULTS \par                  FOR THE YEAR ENDED 31 DECEMBER 2017 \par  \par     SUMMARY \par  \par     For the year ended 31 December 2017 (the "Year"), the turnover from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par     of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Company Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   (the "Company" and \par     together with its subsidiaries, the " Group " ) was approximately RMB6,292,641,000 \par     (2016: RMB5,619,842,000), representing an increase of 12.0% over the previous year. \par     Net profit attributable to the owners of the Company (excluding extraordinary items) \par     was approximately RMB1,338,856,000 (2016: net profit attributable to the owners of \par     the Company (excluding extraordinary items) of approximately RMB1,308,964,000), \par     representing an increase of approximately 2.3% over the previous year. Net profit from \par     continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attributable to the owners of the Company was approximately \par     RMB1,256,484,000 (2016: net profit from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attributable to the owners \par     of the Company (excluding extraordinary items) of approximately RMB1,235,637,000), \par     representing an increase of approximately 1.7% over the previous year. \par  \par     During the Year, Weihai Weigao Blood Purification Products Company Limited ("Weigao \par     Blood Purification " ) issued new shares to its management and some of its existing \par     shareholders and a strategic investor. The shareholding of the Company has been diluted \par     from 70% to 46.875%. Due to the change in the composition of the board of directors of \par     Weigao Blood Purification, the Company no longer controls the board of Weigao Blood \par     Purification. Weigao Blood Purification ceased to be a subsidiary of the Company and is \par     accounted for as an associated company. As such, segment reporting on the manufacturing \par     and sale of blood purification products had been ceased during the Year. \par  \par      For identification purpose only \par * \par  \par                                                               1 \par The existing continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Group are single use consumables, orthopaedic \par products and others. During the Year, the performance of its major business segments was as \par follows: \par  \par  \par (1)   turnover of single use consumables of the Group reached approximately \par       RMB5,422,255,000 for the year ended 31 December 2017, representing an increase of \par       12.6% when compared with the previous year; \par  \par  \par (2)   turnover of orthopaedic products of the Group for the year ended 31 December \par       2017 was approximately RMB870,386,000, representing an increase of 8.3% when \par       compared with the previous year. \par  \par  \par The Directors recommended the payment of a final dividend of RMB0.046 per share \par (2016: RMB0.046), which is subject to the approval by the shareholders of the Company \par ("Shareholders") at the forthcoming general meeting. \par  \par  \par  \par  \pa