, gross profit margin of the Group remained stable at 63.5% (2016: 63.7%). \par With continuous optimization of product mix, management improvement and technology \par updates, the Company was able to offset the rise in product costs caused by the substantial \par increase in raw materials procurement costs. \par  \par  \par 1.   Consumables: the Group recorded a turnover for consumable products of approximately \par      RMB5,422,255,000, representing an increase of 12.6% when compared with the \par      previous year. \par  \par  \par      During the Year, the sales of the Group's specialized infusion sets with precision filter, \par      infusion sets for special use and the infusion sets made of proprietary non-PVC based \par      material continued to grow. The turnover of infusion sets of the Group amounted to \par      approximately RMB1,668,532,000, representing an increase of 6.1% over last year. The \par      Directors believe that specialized infusion sets with precision filter, infusion sets for \par      clinical special use and non-PVC based infusion sets have development potential in the \par      PRC. The Group will continue to consolidate its core competitiveness in this sector. \par  \par      Turnover for needle products of the Group for the Year was approximately \par      RMB1,017,672,000, representing an increase of 13.7% when compared with the \par      previous year. During the Year, in view of the intensive competition from domestic \par      needle products manufacturers, the Company further improved and enhanced its \par      product functionalities, conducted product segmentation and accelerated new products \par      launch, whereby leading to an increase in overall revenue of such products through \par      sales of safety intravenous catheter needles and intravenous catheter needles ancillary \par      consumables. The Company would continue to increase its ongoing investments in \par      needle products to enable such products to remain as one of the important segments for \par      the future development of the Company. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               26 \par      Turnover of syringe products for the Year amounted to approximately RMB859,933,000, \par  \par      representing an increase of 13.5% when compared with previous year. The remarkable \par      growth of radiation-resistant infusion sets and exported syringes led to an increase in the \par      revenue of syringe products. The Board is of the view that there will be a good market \par      development for the radiation-resistant infusion sets because of improvement in product \par      safety and on the environment. \par  \par  \par      Turnover of pre-filled syringes and pre-filled flush syringe products for the Year \par      amounted to approximately RMB717,990,000, representing an increase of 19.9% when \par      compared with previous year. The pre-filled syringes and pre-filled flush syringes \par      achieved optional utilization of production capacity. With advantages of pre-filled \par      syringes in multiple segment markets, it continued to maintain a good growth pace. Pre- \par      filled flush syringes continued to maintain a relatively high growth momentum driving \par      the overall growth of consumables. The Group will continue to maintain a favourable \par      position in such market. \par  \par  \par      Turnover of wound management products for the Year amounted to approximately \par      RMB182,004,000, representing an increase of 6.0% when compared with last year. \par      Market development for anastomat, sutures and functional dressing progressed smoothly \par      with higher sales growth. \par  \par  \par 2.   Orthopaedic business recorded a turnover of approximately RMB870,386,000 during the \par      Year, representing an increase of 8.3% as compared with previous year. During the Year, \par      orthopaedic segment promoted sales growth by establishing regional warehouses and \par      logistics platform and continued launching of new products. With continued launching \par      of spine and joint products to the market, it provided strong supports for sales growth. \par  \par  \par      During the Year, as a result of product mix adjustment, the percentage of turnover \par      from high value-added products under continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (products with gross profit \par      margins over 60%) to total turnover was at 59.7% (2016: 59.6%). \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               27 \par RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT \par  \par For the twelve months ended 31 December 2017, product registration certificates for 29 \par new products under continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were obtained by the Group. The research and \par development for 30 products were completed for which applications for product registration \par certificates are underway. The Group obtained 44 new patents and 76 new patents are under \par application. \par  \par The strategy of placing strong emphasis on research and development has enhanced the \par competitiveness and laid a foundation for the Company to fully leverage on its customer \par resources and provided the Group with new profit growth drivers. \par  \par For the twelve months ended 31 December 2017, the continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Group had \par over 360 product registration certificates and over 440 patents, of which 53 were patents on \par invention. \par  \par In view of the need for the strategic adjustments to product mix, the Group continued to \par increase the investments in the research and development in existing products series and new \par medical devices, so as to further improve its product series and expand product range. The \par Group continued to maintain the leading position in research and development capability \par in China. For the twelve months ended 31 December 2017, total research and development \par expenses from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amounted to approximately RMB273,825,000 (2016: \par approximately RMB266,037,000), representing 4.4% (2016: 4.7%) of the revenue of the \par Group. \par  \par PRODUCTION \par  \par During the Year, in order to constantly expand production capacity, the Group continued to \par expand its production facilities including pre-filled flush syringe workshop and pre-filled \par syringe workshop to satisfy the sales demand for future market growth. \par  \par SALES AND MARKETING \par  \par The Group continually optimized marketing management, built and expanded the sales teams \par of specialized products in the consumables sector and further increased the market share \par of newly launched products.. The Group achieved substantial results in key client accounts \par management. The Group also increased the staff headcount for clinical marketing, placed \par more resources to support market channels and continued to promote hospital administrators \par and medical staff training projects. \par  \par  \par                                              28 \par During the Year, the Group strengthened its sales management system. The Group focused \par on its marketing resources on customer development and maintained the relationship with \par hospitals from the grade-A of tier two or above  As at the date of \par                                                                    . \par this announcement, the continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Group has a total customer base of \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2018 06:55 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  . -9-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par 5,117