 interest expenses from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Group for the year ended 31 \par December 2017 were approximately RMB23,879,000 (2016: approximately RMB25,065,000). \par  \par  \par GEARING RATIO \par  \par As at 31 December 2017, total net cash of the Group amounted to approximately \par RMB2,779,055,000 (2016: RMB2,879,281,000) and the gearing ratio of the Group was 7.5%, \par compared to 10.1% as of the same period last year. The gearing ratio which represents total \par debt as a percentage of total capital. Total debt is calculated as total borrowings. Total capital \par is calculated as the Group's shareholders' fund. \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RISKS \par  \par The Group's purchases and sales are mainly conducted in the PRC. All of its assets, liabilities \par and transactions are denominated in RMB. For the year ended 31 December 2017, the Group \par had not encountered any material difficulty due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuation nor affecting its \par own operating funds. For the twelve months ended 31 December 2017, the Group had no \par significant exposure to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuation or hedging for such risk. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                33 \par Due to the change in exchange rates, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par equivalent to RMB1,883,000 for the year ended 31 December 2017 was recognised (2016: \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loss equivalent to RMB4,056,000) by the Company. \par  \par CONTINGENT LIABILITIES \par  \par The Group had no material contingent liabilities as at 31 December 2017. \par  \par MATERIAL INVESTMENTS/FUTURE MATERIAL INVESTMENT \par PLANS \par  \par 1.   During the Year, the Group continued to invest approximately RMB1,512,637,000 for \par      purchase of properties and production facilities; and for the construction of the Group's \par      medical consumables industrial zone. \par  \par 2.   During the Year, Weihai Weigao Blood Purification Products Company Limited \par      ("Weigao Blood Purification") issued new shares to its management and some of its \par      existing shareholders and a strategic investor. The shareholding of the Company has \par      been diluted from 70% to 46.875%. Due to the change in the composition of the board \par  \par      of directors of Weigao Blood Purification, the Company no longer controls the board of \par      Weigao Blood Purification. Weigao Blood Purification ceased to be a subsidiary of the \par      Company and is accounted for as an associated company. As such, segment reporting on \par      the manufacturing and sale of blood purification products had been ceased during the \par      Year. \par  \par 3.   In 2017, the Group through its 100% wholly owned subsidiary, Weigao International \par      Medical Company Limited ("Weigao International") formed a joint venture ("JV") with \par      an independent third party. The JV is owned as to 90% by Weigao International and \par      10% of the JV partner. On 23 January 2018, the JV completed the acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Argon \par      Medical Devices\f28 \uc2 \f2  Holdings . Inc. ("Argon") for a consideration of US$844.2 million \par      (subject to customary post-closing adjustments) of which US$420 million was debt \par      financing raised by Argon. The remaining 90% of US$424.2 million, being US$381.8 \par      million, was funded by Weigao International from its internal resources. Argon will \par      become one of the core platforms for the overseas expansion of the Group. \par  \par 4.   In 2018, the Group plans to invest approximately RMB250,000,000 for constructing new \par      pre-filled syringe production workshops and purchase of new production lines, which are \par      expected to be in production successively by the end of 2019. \par  \par  \par  \par                                              34 \par 5.   The upgrading and reconfiguration of the single-use consumables production equipment \par      is ongoing in 2018. It is planned that an additional approximately RMB120,000,000 will \par      be invested to further raise the level of production automation. \par  \par  \par Save for the above material investments and investment plans, the Group had no material \par capital commitments or any future plans involving significant investments or capital assets \par acquisition as at 31 December 2017. \par  \par  \par CAPITAL COMMITMENTS \par  \par As at 31 December 2017, the capital commitments of the Group and the Company \par contracted but not provided for in respect of the acquisition of Argon and the acquisition \par of property, plant and equipment amounted to approximately RMB2,948,758,000 (2016: \par RMB643,540,000). The above amounts will be financed by the internal resources of the \par Group. \par  \par PLEDGE OF THE GROUP'S ASSETS \par  \par As at 31 December 2017, the Group did not pledge the land use rights and buildings (2016: \par RMB Nil), but the Group had pledged the equity interest in Weigao Jierui, a wholly-owned \par subsidiary of the Group, to secure the long-term borrowings from \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Finance \par Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  , and pledged bank deposits of RMB96,178,000 (2016: RMB36,980,000) to secure \par the bills and banking facilities granted to the Group. \par  \par  \par RESERVES AND DISTRIBUTABLE RESERVES \par  \par As at 31 December 2017, total reserves of the Group amounted to RMB12,885,938,000 (2016: \par RMB11,414,344,000). \par  \par  \par Under the PRC laws and regulations, the Company's distributable reserves will be based on \par the lower of the amount calculated according to the PRC accounting principles and rules and \par the amount calculated according to the Hong Kong generally accepted accounting principles. \par As at 31 December 2017, the distributable reserves of the Company were approximately \par RMB3,391,686,000 (2016: RMB2,942,314,000). \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                             35 \par REVIEW AND OUTLOOK \par  \par In 2017, by overcoming the impact from various adverse factors such as lower tender prices, \par government policies of price control, in regulating distribution arrangement in medical device \par sector and the rise in production costs, the Company continued to adhere to product mix \par optimisation and adjustment strategy, constantly improved and upgraded product functionality \par and increased investment in technical renovation, with an aim to enhance production \par efficiency, improve product quality and constantly launching new products. In addition to \par enhancing the sales management strategy and integrating marketing resources, sharing of key \par accounts and financing arrangements to facilitate sales as well as implementing staff incentive \par arrangement, the Company continued to maintain growth in revenue and profit despite obvious \par slowdown in industry growth and intensified competition. \par  \par LOOKING FORWARD TO 2018 \par  \par Through proprietary research and development and leveraging on the cooperation with \par research institutes, the Company will strengthen product upgrading and research and \par development capabilities, further strengthening existing product lines, intensify the marketing \par of wound management products, highlight product safety and patient application safety, \par improve patient treatment experience and quicken the pace in launching pipeline products, \par offsetting numerous adverse impacts to maintain its competitive edge. During the Year, the \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2018 06:56 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  . -11-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par Company will reinforce or launch a series of new products including DEHP-free infusion \par sets, radiation-resistant infusion sets, central venous catheters, flush syringes (cyclo olefin \par polymer), orthopedic spines, joints and ultrasonic bone scalpel. \par  \par  \par In view of the effectiveness achieved by key client accounts management, the Company \par will continue such strategy and increase single customer contribution by promoting various \par products via the key accounts management. By developing the financing lease business around \par the Company's industry chain and forming synergies and driving sales between financial \par services and product sales. \par  \par  \par Regarding the in-depth implementation of national medical reform policies such as "two- \par invoice system", proportion control of medical consumables in public hospitals and single- \par disease payment, the Company considers that despite such policies may have adverse impact \par on the financial performance to a certain extent in the short term, however, they will facilitate \par industry concentration and increase the market share of domestic branded products in the \par long-term and benefit the growth of outstanding enterprises in the industry. \par  \par  \par  \par                                                36 \par As overseas market is the focus of our medium and long-term strategic plan, the Company \par will proactively develop its overseas business layout and proceed with marketable product \par registration in target market, gradually establish long-term stable sales channel and network, \par and explore the production and marketing pattern in overseas market. The proportion of sales \par in overseas markets to the total revenue of the Group is expected to increase gradually. \par  \par  \par The acquisition of Argon has been successfully completed. At the strategic level, Argon will \par become the Group's platform for overseas expansion and play an active role in technological \par upgrade, product innovation and mergers and acquisitions. At the business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level, \par the Group will formulate a plan with the management team of Argon to implement the sale \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventional\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  products in the market in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The management considers that Argon as a \par part of Weigao will make an important contribution to the long-term stable development of the \par Group. \par  \par  \par The Company will continue to improve and extend existing product lines and introduce \par advanced technologies through equity investments and mergers and acquisitions. \par  \par  \par While continuously carrying out automation and supply chain management improvement \par in production, the Company will continue to improve its product quality and to, increase \par production efficiency to maintain cost advantages. \par  \par  \par By relying on its enriched product lines and solid research and development advantages, \par continue to launch new products and improve product upgrades, insist on adapting to market \par and future-oriented operating strategy, and motivate employee creativity, the management \par believes that the Company will continue to maintain its leading position in the PRC \par market. Meanwhile, the Company will proactively develop overseas business to achieve the \par coordinated development of domestic and foreign markets, supporting the stable growth in the \par operating results of the Group. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               37 \par SHARE AWARD SCHEME REGARDING NON-LISTED SHARES OF THE \par COMPANY \par  \par As approved on the extraordinary general meeting and class meetings on 17 November 2014 \par (the "Adoption Date"), the Company adopted a share award scheme (the "Scheme") regarding \par a specific mandate to issue a maximum of 223,818,616 Non-listed Shares as incentive shares \par under the Scheme. The 223,818,616 Non-listed Shares represent 5% of the issued share \par capital of the Company or approximately 4.76% of the issued share capital of the Company \par as enlarged by the issue of the 223,818,616 Non-listed Shares on the Adoption Date. The \par incentive shares allotted to the eligible participants will be subject to a lock-up period and \par performance target based on certain key performance indicators. The Scheme serves to retain \par the long-term service of the selected employee and align his/her continuous performance with \par the development goal of the Group. Details of the Scheme are set out in the circular of the \par Company dated 30 September 2014. \par  \par  \par On 11 December 2015, the Company granted 45,960,000 incentive shares to 111 selected \par employees. On 4 January 2016, the trustees subscribed the shares with the consideration of \par RMB101,112,000 at the grant price of RMB2.20 per share. \par  \par LOAN AGREEMENT WITH INTERNATIONAL FINANCE \par CORPORATION \par  \par On 27 January 2015, the Company entered into a five (5) years loan agreement (the "Loan \par Agreement") for the principal amount of RMB600 million (approximately HK$672 million) \par (the "Loan") with the International Finance Corporation ("IFC"), a member of the World \par  \par Bank Group and the largest global development institution focused exclusively on the private \par sector. The Loan is repayable in one lump sum on 15 March 2020. The Loan is jointly secured \par by 100% equity interest of Jierui that owned by the Company and 230,000,000 shares of the \par Company that owned by Weigao Holding. Details of the Loan Agreement are set out in the \par announcement of the Company dated 27 January 2015. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                              38 \par EVENT AFTER REPORTING PERIOD \par  \par On 22 September 2017, the JV entered into an agreement to acquire 100% equity interest \par in Argon. On 23 January 2018, the JV completed the acquisition of Argon Medical Devices \par Holdings. Inc. ("Argon") for a consideration of US$844.2 million (subject to customary \par post-closing adjustments) of which US$420 million was debt financing raised by Argon. \par The remaining 90% of US$424.2 million, being US$381.8 million, was funded by Weigao \par International from its internal resources. Details of the acquisition are set out in the Group's \par announcements dated 24 September 2017 and 24 January 2018. The initial accounting for \par the business combination is incomplete at the time the consolidated financial statements are \par authorised for issue. The fair value of the assets and liabilities of Argon is still under review. \par Argon focuses mainly in the high-end biopsy, vascular and drainage medical devices with \par multiple physician-preference products. \par  \par PURCHASE, SALE OR REDEMPTION OF THE COMPANY'S LISTED \par SECURITIES \par  \par During the Year, there was no purchase, sale or redemption of its securities by the Company or \par any of its subsidiaries. \par  \par  \par BOARD PRACTICES AND PROCEDURES \par  \par The Code on Corporate Governance Practices (the "CCGP") contained in the Listing Rules \par which set out the principles of good corporate governance and the Company is required \par to comply with the code provisions of the CCGP. The Company fully admitted that good \par corporate governance, as part of the Company's culture, can create values to the Group and \par the Shareholders efficiently. The Board is committed to continuing to enhance the standards of \par corporate governance within the Group and to ensure that the Group conducts its businesses \par in an honest and responsible manner. The Group has adopted practices which meets the code \par provisions of the CCGP. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                39 \par CHANGE OF BOARD COMPOSITION AND SENIOR MANAGEMENT \par  \par 1.   Mr. Cui Jin has resigned as the Chief Financial Officer of the Company with effect from \par      17 February 2017. \par  \par  \par 2.   Mr. Wu Xue Feng has been appointed as the Chief Financial Officer of the Company \par      with effect from 17 February 2017. \par  \par  \par      Mr. Xia Lie Bo \par  \par 3.                      has resigned as an executive Director with effect from 4 \par      December 2017. \par  \par COMPLIANCE WITH THE MODEL CODE FOR DIRECTORS' \par SECURITIES TRANSACTIONS \par  \par The Company has adopted the Model Code as set out in Appendix 10 of the Listing Rules \par as the standard for securities transactions by Directors. The Company has made enquiries of \par all the Directors and all the Directors confirmed that they have complied with the required \par standards set out in the Model Code and its code of conduct regarding directors' securities \par transactions. \par  \par  \par INTERNAL CONTROL \par  \par Directors are responsible for reviewing the internal control and risk management system of \par the Company periodically to ensure its effectiveness and efficiency. With the support of the \par internal audit department, they will review the practices, procedures, expenditure and internal \par control of the Company and its subsidiaries on a regular basis. The management will regularly \par monitor the concerns as reported by the internal audit department to ensure appropriate \par remedial measures have been implemented. The Board or senior management can also request \par the internal audit group to review the specific scope of concerns and report the significant \par findings of such review to the Board and the audit committee. The Board has conducted a \par review of the effectiveness of the system of internal control of the Group. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                               40 \par AUDIT COMMITTEE \par  \par The Audit Committee of the Company comprises three independent non-executive directors, \par namely Mr. Lo Wai Hung, Mrs. Fu Ming Zhong and Mrs. Wang Jin Xia and one non-executive \par Director, namely Mrs. Zhou Shu Hua. The Chairman of the Audit Committee is Mr. Lo \par Wai Hung. The Audit Committee has reviewed the Group's audited consolidated financial \par statements for the Year which have been agreed by the Company's auditor, and is of the \par view that the Group's audited consolidated financial statements for the Year are prepared in \par accordance with the applicable accounting standards, laws and regulations, and appropriate \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2018 06:56 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From Shandong Weigao Group Medical Polymer Co. Ltd. -12-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par disclosures have already been made. The Audit Committee has also reviewed the annual \par results for the Year. \par  \par CONFIRMATION OF INDEPENDENCE OF THE INDEPENDENT NON \par EXECUTIVE DIRECTORS \par  \par The Company confirmed that it had received the annual confirmation of independence from \par each of the Independent Non-executive Directors in compliance with Rule 3.13 of the Listing \par Rules on 27 March 2018. The Company is of the view that the Independent Non-executive \par Directors remain independent during the Year in accordance with the relevant requirements of \par Rule 3.13 of the Listing Rules. \par  \par  \par PRE-EMPTIVE RIGHTS \par  \par There are no provisions for pre-emptive right under the Company's articles of association and \par the laws of the PRC, which would oblige the Company to offer new shares on a pro-rata basis \par to existing shareholders. \par  \par  \par CORPORATE GOVERNANCE \par  \par The Company is committed to maintain high standards of corporate governance so as to \par ensure better transparency and protection of shareholders ' interest. The Company has \par complied with the code provision of the Code on Corporate Governance Practices (the \par "Code") in Appendix 14 of the Listing Rules throughout the year ended 31 December 2017. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                              41 \par ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING AND CLOSURE OF REGISTER OF \par MEMBERS \par  \par Attending and Voting in the Annual General Meeting \par  \par  \par In order to determine the shareholders who are entitled to attend and vote at the Annual \par General Meeting, the register of members of the Company for both H Shares and Non-listed \par Shares will be closed from Saturday, 19 May 2018 to Monday, 18 June 2018 (both days \par inclusive), during which period no transfer of H Shares or Non-listed Shares will be effected. \par In order to qualify for attending and voting in the Annual General Meeting, Shareholders \par should ensure that all transfer documents, accompanied by the relevant share certificates, are \par lodged with the Company's H Share registrar, Tricor Standard Limited, at Level 22, Hopewell \par Centre, 183 Queen's Road East, Hong Kong for registration no later than 4:30 p.m. on Friday, \par 18 May 2018. \par  \par  \par In order to qualify for attending and voting in the Annual General Meeting:- \par  \par  \par Latest time to lodge in transfer \par   instrument accompanied \par   by the share certificates for H Shares . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 4:30 p.m., Friday, \par                                                                                                      18 May 2018 \par  \par Closure of register of members of \par   the Company for attending and voting \par   in the Annual General Meeting . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Saturday, 19 May 2018 to \par                                                                                        Monday, 18 June 2018 \par                                                                                          (both days inclusive) \par  \par  \par Latest time to lodge in the reply slip . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Tuesday, 29 May 2018 \par  \par  \par Date of the Annual General Meeting . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Tuesday, 19 June 2018 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                         42 \par Entitlement of Proposed Final dividend \par  \par  \par In order to determine entitlement to the proposed final dividend payment, the register of \par members of the Company for both H Shares and Non-listed Shares will be closed from \par Saturday, 23 June 2018 to Thursday, 28 June 2018 (both days inclusive), during which \par period no transfer of H Shares or Non-listed Shares will be effected. In order to qualify for \par entitlement of the proposed final dividend, holders of H Shares should ensure that all transfer \par documents, accompanied by the relevant share certificates, are lodged with the Company's \par H Share registrar, Tricor Standard Limited, at 22/F, Hopewell Centre, 183 Queen's Road East, \par Wanchai, Hong Kong for registration no later than 4:30 p.m. on Friday, 22 June 2018. \par  \par  \par In order to qualify to entitle the final dividend for the year ended 31 December 2017:- \par  \par Latest time to lodge in transfer instrument accompanied \par   by the share certificates for H Shares . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 4:30 p.m., Friday, \par                                                                                                      22 June 2018 \par  \par Closure of register of members of \par   the Company for entitlement of \par   the final dividend for the \par   year ended 31 December 2017. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . Saturday, 23 June 2018 to \par                             