se income tax for such non-resident enterprise shareholders. Therefore, as a \par PRC domestic enterprise, the Company will, after withholding 10% of the final dividend as \par enterprise income tax, distribute the final dividend to non-resident enterprise shareholders, i.e. \par any shareholders who hold the Company's shares in the name of non-individual shareholders, \par including but not limited to HKSCC Nominees Limited, other nominees, trustees, or holders \par of H Shares registered in the name of other organizations and groups. \par  \par                                                  the \par Pursuant to the PRC Individual Income Tax Law                                           , \par  \par Implementation Regulations of the PRC Individual Income Tax Law \par  the Notice of the State Administration of Taxation in relation to \par                            , \par the Administrative Measures on Preferential Treatment Entitled by Non-residents under Tax \par  \par Treaties (Tentative) (Guo Shui Fa [2009] No. 124) \par                        [2009]124 (the "Tax Treaties \par                                                                        ) \par Notice"), the Notice of the State Administration of Taxation on the Questions Concerning the \par Levy and Administration of Individual Income Tax After the Repeal of Guo Shui Fa [1993] \par                                                      [1993]045 \par No. 45 (Guo Shui Han [2011] No. 348) \par                    [2011]348 , other relevant laws \par  \par and regulations and other regulatory documents, the Company shall, as a withholding agent, \par withhold and pay individual income tax for the individual holders of H shares in respect \par of the dividend to be distributed to them. However, the individual holders of H shares may \par be entitled to certain tax preferential treatments pursuant to the tax treaties between the \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                44 \p