\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 China appointed \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  governor of the  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 China on Monday confirmed its desire for economic opening with the appointment of reformist \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  as the new governor of its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is expected to continue on the modernizing path of its predecessor, \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite being number two and Zhou's right-hand man, Yi did not figure in the bets on who could succeed the governor of the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , so his appointment, decided on Monday by the plenary of the National People's Assembly, was received With surprise.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, the appointment of Liu He, economic adviser and ally of President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , to the position of vice prime minister of finance and planning, was expected, a position of maximum responsibility that will also be decisive for the management of commercial relations. with the United States and the economic opening.\par \par \uc2 "The main task (of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) right now is to implement a prudent monetary policy, promote the reform of the financial sector, its opening and maintain the stability of the sector," Yi told the press shortly after his appointment was made public in the Great Palace of the People in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 His pro-reformist profile and his extensive training abroad seem to indicate that Yi (60-year-old Pekinese) will continue on the modernizing path initiated by Zhou and will encourage the opening of finance to investment from abroad.\par \par \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  is considered a leader "with very deep international ties," said Jinyue Dong, BBVA Research economist. In his opinion, the election of Yi is a sign that China "will promote financial liberalization and liberalization, as well as connect the domestic financial sector with the world, in particular by promoting dialogue between China and the West", while at the same time perpetuates its monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Yi studied Economics for two years at \uc2 Peking University\uc2 , then Business Administration at the University of Hamline (Minnesota, USA) and Economics at the \uc2 University of Illinois\uc2 , where she also studied her PhD specialized in the selection of statistical models.\par \par \uc2 In 1986 he began his career as a professor at the University of Indiana, a position he left in 1994 to return to China and join as a professor at Peking University.\par \par \uc2 He joined the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  in 1997 and, five years later, was appointed Secretary General of its Monetary Policy Committee. From that position he led the reform of rural financial institutions in 2004 and in 2007 he was appointed deputy governor.\par \par \uc2 From 2009 to 2016 he led the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was in charge of the reform of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system and the diversification of its investments.\par \par \uc2 In addition, he was involved in the research and design of the reform of the Chinese social security system and is recognized for his determination to help the poorest strata of society.\par \par \uc2 It is also attributed to having asked the government, already in 2002, not only to take care of the growth of the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of the country, but to take into account factors such as employment, the environment and the indebtedness of the banks. .\par \par \uc2 His appointment coincided on Monday with the rise of Liu He to the level of the country's economic vice premier. "Liu and Yi are expected to lead the Chinese financial sector," said Dong, who recalled that since Xi came to power in 2012, Yi served as Liu He's right-hand man.\par \par \uc2 The latter, 66, studied at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  and his role in the Chinese economy recently increased. In January, he \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's representative at the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, one year after President Xi himself; In February he traveled to the US to analyze the economic and trade relations between both countries, in acritical moment for bilateral ties.\par \par \uc2 "Possibly Liu He is the most important economic legislator in the world (...) He was granted the honor of being the only spokesman to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in one of the main Davos sessions without being a national leader," Matthew Dobbs said in an analysis. , manager of Asian equities of the British Schroders.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180321ee3k003v2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
