\par\par \b \uc2 *China Actual Interest Rates Steady, Money Supply Demand Balanced - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Official\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 03:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:14 ET *China to Reduce Reliance on Using Massive Money Support to Stimulate Economic Growth - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Official\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:22 ET *China to Step Up Opening Up of Financial Market- \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Official\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:27 ET *Size of China \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reserves to Remain Stable - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Official\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:28 ET *China to Ease Restrictions on Capital Account in 'Gradual, Steady' Manner - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Official\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:31 ET *\uc2 China \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Play 'More Important' Role in Financial Supervision - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Chief\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:38 ET *PBOC Chief Says Time Needed to Observe , Indicating No Sweeping Consolidation for Now\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:53 ET *PBOC Chief: M2 Growth Not Accurate Indicator to Measure Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 21:55 ET *PBOC Chief: Need to Pay More Attention to Inflation, Employment\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 22:04 ET *PBOC Chief: Working With Others to Develop Own Digital \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 22:22 ET *PBOC Chief: Still Exploring Regulation Policies on Virtual \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 22:29 ET *\uc2 China \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Working on Regulations Governing Financial-Holding Firms - Official\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 22:42 ET *PBOC Chief: Respects Hong Kong Autonomy Over HK Dollar; Won't \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 8 Mar 2018 22:44 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 China Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Remarks From Briefing During National People's Congress\par \par \uc2 9 Mar 2018 00:23 ET  China \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Play 'More Important' Role in Financial Supervision\par \par \uc2 BEIJING--\uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will play a more important role in financial supervision as the authorities streamline financial regulation, but they need more time to decide on the direction, \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan said Friday, suggesting sweeping changes won't be imminent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fill a vacuum in regulatory supervision as China tries to improve efficiency and coordination among regulators, Mr. Zhou said at a briefing during the National People's Congress.\par \par \uc2 "We have studied the 'twin peaks' [regulatory structure,] but we still need time to observe. We won't necessarily adopt the 'twin peaks'," he said, referring to a model of financial regulation in countries including the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 Under that regulatory model, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is responsible for financial stability and prudential issues, while a separate agency oversees business issues and investor protection.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Zhou vowed to step up efforts to ease restrictions on China's financial market to make it more accessible for foreign investors, while repeating a long-standing policy goal of liberalizing the capital account in a gradual and steady manner.\par \par \uc2 China will reduce its reliance on pumping large amounts of cash into the domestic economy to stimulate growth, he said.\par \par \uc2 M2 growth is no longer an accurate barometer of China's monetary policy, he said, adding the authorities will pay more attention to other indicators such as inflation and employment.\par \par \uc2 China's consumer inflation accelerated to a more-than four-year high in February, as food prices rose for the first time in over a year on demand during the Lunar New Year holiday, official data showed Friday. The consumer-price index rose 2.9% from a year earlier in February, close to Beijing's 2018 target ceiling of 3%.\par \par \uc2 They country's broadest measure of money supply, M2, also released Friday, grew 8.8% at the end of February from a year earlier, compared with an 8.6% increase at the end of January.\par \par \uc2 At Friday's briefing, Mr. Zhou said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working with other agencies to develop its own digital \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but needs to conduct tests before rolling out any digital \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Liyan Qi at liyan.qi@wsj.com and Chao Deng at chao.deng@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 09, 2018 00:23 ET (05:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180309ee39000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
