\par\par \b \uc2 Trade-War Fears Could Trigger PBoC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 09:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0852 GMT - As \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell last month for the first time in a year, the reason was falling asset values because of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings amid February's market tumult, says Julian Evans-Pritchard at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  . Meanwhile, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely stayed on the sidelines. But he sees capital outflows likely picking up later this year as Beijing may need to cut interest rates in response to anticipated slower economic growth. Meanwhile, US protectionism could weaken global investor appetite for emerging-market assets. "If the \uc2 PBoC\uc2  has learnt the lessons from the renminbi panic a couple of years ago, they will promptly step up \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening too rapidly." (grace.zhu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT - \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under little pressure to raise rates further this year partly because the inflation has slowed substantially and the economy has cooled, says \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  , following the bank's stand-pat decision Wednesday. Further rate increases could also put further upward pressure on the ringgit, which is already up 15% against the US dollar since last year's low, it says. Additional appreciation could damage the competitiveness of the country's export sector, it adds. (chester.yung@wsj.com; @chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT - Taiwan economic data produce a couple of surprises as the Lunar New Year again leaves economists with egg on their faces. Inflation in February, the month of the holiday, accelerated to 2.2%, the highest since January 2016, when consumer prices were also jacked up by festive demand. For both January and February, price growth averaged 1.5%, closer to December's figure but which still indicates a general recent pickup in inflation. Meanwhile, analysts were further off the mark on trade data that showed a 1.2% fall in exports compared with an expected gain of 7.4%. It's the first slip since in overseas shipments since September 2016 as semiconductor exports fell 4.8%. (paul.jackson@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0836 GMT - The 2028-dated government bond may attract the most interest from investors among the three bonds on offer at the \uc2 Czech finance ministry\uc2  's bond auction Wednesday, Komercni analyst Dalimil Vyskovsky says. The 2033-dated bond is probably too long for many investors, while the 2023-dated debt is "still being a bit too low in yield to spark much interest," Vyskovsky says. The ministry offers maximum CZK4 billion in each bond. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0831 GMT - \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  's policy statement today reaffirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's positive outlook on growth and repeated that this year's inflation should average less than 2017. ANZ says the only change from January's statement was a reference to the need for a policy stance that prevents the buildup of financial risks being dropped. The firm notes today's pronouncement instead rather emphasized that current policy is consistent with steady economic growth and lower inflation. ANZ still expects another 2018 rate hike in September after January's move. (yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com; @yantoultra)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT - Italy, which held elections on Sunday, lines up for scheduled reviews by \uc2 Fitch\uc2  and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  on March 16. While \uc2 Moody's\uc2  may well wait to see what form the next government in Italy takes, "it could also act on its outlook outside of the usual calendar, as it did with Greece recently," says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  rates strategist Ciaran O'Hagan. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  holds Italy at 'Baa2' with a negative outlook. \uc2 Fitch\uc2 , which has 'BBB' rating with stable outlook on Italy, said Tuesday that the general election result increases the likelihood of some fiscal loosening in Italy, and further weakens the prospect for structural economic reforms. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT - The dollar falls early Wednesday after the resignation of U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's chief economic advisor \uc2 Gary Cohn\uc2  reignited trade war fears as Cohn had opposed trade tariffs. USD/JPY is down 0.4% at 105.68, and EUR/USD up marginally at 1.2408. However, the dollar rises against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of countries heavily reliant on trade with the U.S. USD/CAD rises 0.4% to 1.2929 and USD/MXN rises 0.5% to 18.8287. Commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also fall, with AUD/USD down 0.4% at 0.7802. "We are wary of unchecked protectionist forces turning to the USD as a policy tool," \uc2 RBC\uc2  says. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0806 GMT - The recent slide in India's private sector banks creates great entry opportunities as stress asset cases are largely recognized and credit demand is getting better, says Jefferies. In addition, bids for the \uc2 RBI\uc2 's first list of large stressed loans is coming in much better than expected, a factor that should help cushion provision impact for other insolvency cases. Strong retail loan growth, a service sector recovery and improvement in corporate credit is driving overall bank credit growth of more than 10% in recent months, the investment bank says. The street is not pricing in an earnings recovery or is too narrowly focused on near term asset-quality issues, it adds. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0759 GMT - Eurozone government bonds edge slightly higher as investors look ahead to Thursday's \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's meeting, which \uc2 KBC\uc2  says could subdue trade on Wednesday. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  also says shaky risk sentiment on the resignation of U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's chief economic advisor \uc2 Gary Cohn\uc2  could provide support to Bunds. The 10-year bund yield is trading at 0.66%, down about 1 basis point, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  rates strategist Michael Leister says while the recovery in peripheral bonds may stall this morning amid the general risk-off tone, "the overall resilience is remarkable." \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  considers setbacks as better buying opportunities. Supply pressure looks to be limited in the eurozone with only Germany lining up with an EUR4 billion tap of the April 2023 bobl. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0747 GMT - London stocks are expected to open lower, along with other European stocks, after the resignation of President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's top economic adviser \uc2 Gary Cohn\uc2  , who had opposed Trump's plan for tariffs on steel and aluminum. The FTSE 100 is expected to open 50 points lower at 7096, according to \uc2 London Capital Group\uc2  . Cohn's resignation "leads to the conclusion that Trump has won and is serious about his tariffs," says \uc2 Jasper Lawler\uc2 , head of research at LCG. Housebuilders will be watched when Halifax house price data is released at 0830 GMT. Shares in Rolls-Royce in focus after results, as well as \uc2 NMC Health\uc2  , \uc2 Paddy Power Betfair\uc2  and \uc2 Legal & General\uc2  . Packaging stocks will stay in focus following Tuesday's bid for \uc2 Smurfit Kappa\uc2  by \uc2 International Paper Co\uc2  ., with \uc2 DS Smith\uc2  releasing a trading update. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0646 GMT - \uc2 IL&FS Transportation Networks\uc2  has scrapped a possible $300 million debt sale, indicating tougher investor expectation as supply of Asian dollar bonds picks up. The 5-year deal, which was to price last night, got orders in excess of the issue size but not strong enough to tighten the initial 7% pricing, according to a person familiar with the matter. Analysts say the market is still shaky from last month's selloff, meaning investors continue to demand a premium. The Indian issuer, which raised $138 million at 8% from a dim-sum bond last month, was to use the funds for lending to infrastructure projects there. IL&FS shares are down 3.4% today, putting the year's slump at 19% and at fresh record lows. (manju.dalal@wsj.com; @manjudalalsg)\par \par \uc2 0630 GMT - The latest government-work report provides good visibility on China's property market, says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  , as policy differentiation continues across the country. The unlikelihood of a homogeneous property tax and improvement in housing inventory should offer good protection to home prices, the investment bank believes. It also thinks the government will continue to support end-user and urbanization demand. With a 16% pulling in the sector's stocks the past 5 weeks, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  sees Hong Kong-listed developers including CR Land and \uc2 Shimao\uc2  as attractive with potential of earnings-forecast upgrades. (john.wu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 07, 2018 03:52 ET (08:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180307ee37000zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
