\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves Data Prove Absence of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2018\par 12:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1102 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves suggest that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the yuan's recent gains against the dollar, says Mark Williams of Capital Economics . All the increase in the value of reserves are due to changes in exchange rates and market pricing, he says. "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  's recent inactivity is striking" as Beijing has rarely been quite so sanguine about sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves against the dollar in the past, he says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has probably become more subtle in managing exchange rates, trying to stay away from heavy-handed market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1040 GMT - \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  's 2018 guidance--while seemingly in line with consensus--is disappointing upon further reflection because it implies "weaker underlying operating performance projections" than expected, Berenberg says. \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  expects 2018 core EPS growth of 2% to 5% at constant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a negative \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of 3% to 4%. This implies flat EPS growth this year, the bank says, which is "broadly in line with consensus." However, Berenberg says \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  that calculated \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact based on December, so the headwind is likely to be bigger because of the euro's subsequent strengthening. Furthermore, \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  's 2018 tax rate is lower than expected, and guidance already includes recent acquisitions, so the underlying situation may be weaker than it first appears, Berenberg says. (sonia.amaralrohter@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1027 GMT - The recent jump in European government bond yields, which has stalled this week on equity volatility, has been a "good rise" for the corporate bond market, \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  strategists say. Higher sovereign yields push corporate yields higher, prompting insurance companies to buy more corporate bonds. This has helped the spread between corporate and government bond yields tighten "impressively" year-to-date, the strategists say. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 1024 GMT - \uc2 Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's decision to hold policy rates steady came as no surprise, but it sounded notably more hawkish, says \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  . The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  raised its inflation forecast for the next financial year, while remaining bullish on the growth prospects. \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said this supports its view that rate hikes are likely later this year. However, \uc2 RBI\uc2  will be wary of choking off the recovery too early, it adds. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT - \uc2 Novartis\uc2  bonds lose ground on the secondary market Wednesday as the Swiss pharmaceutical offers three new euro-denominated bonds, aiming to raise at least EUR1.5 billion. Bid asset swap spreads on the 0.625% 2028 euro issue jump to 5.382 basis points from 0.773 bps, based on \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  data. Spreads on other issues--in several cases negative--also widen. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0959 GMT - Eurozone 10-year government bond yield spreads over German bunds trade up to nine basis points tighter. Portugal--whose yield spread over bunds trade 9 basis points tighter at 113 basis points--leads the moves, followed by a narrowing of more than 6 basis point in Italian spreads--at 129 basis points--and Spanish spreads--at 73 basis points, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  data. The contained nature of moves in eurozone peripheral sovereign government bond yields, which showed limited reaction to Tuesday's sharp equity falls, is a "particularly bullish signal," say \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  strategists. This indicates peripheral bonds have decorrelated to some "very significant degree" from risky assets more broadly. Investors should therefore be emboldened to initiate long positions or add to their long holdings in these assets once the dust settles.(emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT - With focus on sharp slides in equity markets on Tuesday, data showing a "notable deterioration" in the U.S. trade balance in December "slipped under the radar," say \uc2 MUFG\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts. \uc2 MUFG\uc2  views the likely widening of the U.S. twin deficits as "structural negatives for the US dollar in the medium to long-term." The data showed the U.S. posted its largest monthly trade deficit in nine years in December as it widened to a seasonally adjusted $53.1 billion. The widening trend is likely to remain in place in coming years and could heighten concerns about Donald Trump 's administration implementing protectionist trade policies, \uc2 MUFG\uc2  says. EUR/USD last down 0.1% at 1.2360. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0916 GMT - \uc2 Novartis\uc2  offers three euro benchmark bonds Wednesday but there's talk that neither the issuer nor the sector offers much relative value. An asset manager says higher-rated, longer-dated bonds in the pharmaceutical sector don't pay much for the risk investors assume. Meanwhile, LBBW analyst Timo Kuerschner wrote in a recent note that \uc2 Novartis\uc2  bonds look expensive for their rating. The Swiss group offers a 5.5-year bond at initial price talk of 15 basis points above mid-swaps, a 12.5-year tranche at 30 bps over and a 20.5-year issue at 40 bps over. It plans to raise EUR500-750 million with each tranche. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT - The drop in the value of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  's foreign reserves last month point to steep losses at the start of 2018. The \uc2 SNB\uc2 's reserves fell by 12.8 billion francs ($13.7 billion) from December. Because the \uc2 SNB\uc2  doesn't appear to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent months, this drop largely represents valuation losses on its massive holdings of foreign stocks and bonds, driven by higher bond yields and a stronger franc in January. By comparison, the \uc2 SNB\uc2  earned a 54 billion franc profit in 2017, so January's loss is only giving back a fraction of that. \uc2 SNB\uc2  shares--the \uc2 SNB\uc2  is only of the only central banks with a listed stock--up nearly 8% early Wednesday. (brian.blackstone@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1001 GMT - ING says the dip in GBP/USD to below 1.40 is "a good buying opportunity" amid a structurally weak dollar backdrop. It says there is risk of a "more hawkish tilt" from the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  on Thursday, even though it won't result in "material GBP upside" until a Brexit transition deal looks more definitive. ING says it continues to target a rise to 1.45 in 1Q "as the U.K. economy regains some of its cyclical swagger." It also says it believes Brexit dynamics "have not been the driving force" behind sterling's recent falls, despite heightened risks of a "hard" Brexit. GBP/USD last down 0.1% on the day at 1.3940, but above the three-week low of 1.3837 reached Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  's foreign reserves tumbled to 731.4 billion francs ($781.6 billion) in January from 744.2 billion francs in December. The drop was likely due to the higher global bond yields last month and a stronger franc, which weakened the value of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets. Euro trading at 1.1584 francs, down slightly from Tuesday. (brian.blackstone@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0848 GMT - Demand for long-end Czech government bonds in the secondary market on Tuesday "poses odds in favor of the issuer" at Wednesday's auction of three lines, says Komercni analyst Dalimil Vyskovsky. It is still unlikely there would be a "major chase" for the bonds, compared with recent patterns, he says. The \uc2 Czech finance ministry\uc2  is auctioning bonds due in September 2022, February 2027 and May 2030, offering maximum CZK2 billion, maximum CZK4 billion and maximum CZK4 billion, respectively. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 07, 2018 06:02 ET (11:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180207ee27001dr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
