\par\par \b \uc2 Why Chinese Could Be Ok With Stronger CNY -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2018\par 14:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0856 ET - The Chinese aren't weakening the remnibi when the dollar falls because China is refocusing to a consumer-led economy, and a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brings smaller import prices, which then increases households' real income, says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  . A stronger remnibi also reduces the value of Chinese corporates' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debt, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  says. USD/CNY falls by 0.2% to 6.2723 after reaching a new two-and-a-half-year low around 6.2525 earlier. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0828 ET - The German coalition agreement between the Christian Democrats and the Social Democrats plans "vast" additional expenditure and some revenue shortfalls for this legislative period in Germany, says \uc2 Joerg Kraemer\uc2 , chief economist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . The additional expenditure and revenue shortfalls would reduce the budget surplus by a total of EUR67 billion, he says. The government, in its policy for Europe, will move closer to the redistribution ideas of French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  and \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President \uc2 Jean-Claude Juncker\uc2  , Kraemer says.\par \par \uc2 (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0758 ET - The Chinese remnibi appreciates further against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, taking USD/CNY to a new two-and-a-half-year low of 6.2525, but "China is not taking steps to fully counter a weaker USD," says \uc2 BMO Financial Group\uc2  . In fact, the remnibi has strengthened versus the dollar by as much as the broad dollar value fell in January. USD/CNY was at around 6.53 at the beginning of January and is last trading down 0.2% at 6.2685. "Despite the risk-off environment, which has seen most EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffer, the CNY has been remarkably resilient," \uc2 BMO\uc2  says. On Wednesday, the dollar rises against all major EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , except the remnibi. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0755 ET - The substance of the compromises between the German Christian Democratic Union, Christian Social Union and the Social Democratic Party "may turn out to be expensive over time," says \uc2 Florian Hense\uc2 , an economist at Berenberg. He refers to points such as more generous pension entitlements and small-scale reversals of reforms to the labor market and the financing of the healthcare system. However, with a strengthening economy and a fiscal surplus, "they won't make a material difference to the economic and financial market outlook for the next few years," Hense says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0747 ET - If investors have any concerns regarding the Italy's general elections, they certainly don't show it in the corporate bond market. Option-adjusted spreads on Italian corporate bonds have tightened 12.25% year-to-date, beating the tightening recorded in French, German and Spanish bonds, according to Bloomberg Barclays indexes. The vote is scheduled for March 4. The spread between Italian and German yields has also tightened year-to-date. But one factor indicating Italian political concerns is the recent rise in the probability of an Italian exit from the eurozone, according to Sentix's investor survey-based index. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0740 ET - Uncertainty caused by the U.K.'s vote to leave the EU is "holding the property market to ransom", says property lender Octane Capital after industry data showed prices falling for the second month in a row in January. Prices last month dropped 0.6% against a year earlier, following a 0.8% decline in December, the Halifax House Price Index showed. "While the lack of supply and low borrowing costs rule out a material deterioration in prices, the cost of living and caution around the UK's exit from the EU are starting to get the upper hand," says \uc2 Jonathan Samuels\uc2 , Chief Executive of property lender Octane Capital. "Short of any major breakdowns in negotiations or shock rate rises, the year is shaping up to be flat and uneventful." (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0726 ET - The New Zealand dollar could rise back to 0.74 versus the U.S. dollar in the North American trading session if the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  hints later that it may be "willing to consider tightening this year rather than next, as most market analysts predict," according to BK Asset Management. The \uc2 RBNZ\uc2  announces a decision at 2000 GMT and is expected to keep its main policy rate unchanged at 1.75%. Traders "will be looking for any clues as to when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may begin to resume tightening monetary policy," says BK. NZD/USD last down 0.4% at 0.7307.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0719 ET - Synchronized, broad-based global growth should support emerging market bonds in 2018, says NN Investment Partners which sees the expected returns on the various asset classes in EM bonds between 4% and 8% this year. Within this range, local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds are likely to be at the upper end of this forecast, NN IP says. This year \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and high real rates will determine the large part of the high single-digit total return forecast by NN IP on the EM Local Bond Index. NN IP adds that local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  EM bonds closed 2017 with a 15.2% gain of which 5.8% came from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains against the U.S. dollar, while the remainder was a combination of carry and bond performance. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0714 ET - A fall in EUR/USD is evidence that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are nervous after the sharp equity sell-off earlier this week, says Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Nordea\uc2  in Copenhagen. "The upward momentum in euro/dollar has been put on hold," he says, as EUR/USD trades down 0.3% at 1.2344, having traded higher earlier Wednesday. "The market doesn't know if this [equity fall] is over or if it is the start of something bigger." If the equity slide resumes then the dollar would strengthen. This risk makes investors "hesitant to put on long euro/dollar positions." GBP/USD down 0.4% at 1.3889, but the safe haven yen gains, with USD/JPY down 0.3% at 109.21. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0622 ET - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Iceland\uc2  kept its main rate on hold at 4.25% Wednesday, which comes as little surprise given the recent rise in inflation has been due to temporary exchange rate effects, says \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  . "But with further rises in inflation set to put upward pressure on inflation expectations ahead of this year's wage negotiations, we think that the consensus is underestimating the likelihood of interest rate hikes in the next couple of years." \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  expects the bank to keep interest rates on hold as inflation picks up this year, but then react to the outcome of the wage negotiations by raising interest rates in the autumn. \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  expects the seven-day term deposit rate to hit 5.25% by 3Q 2019. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0602 ET - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves suggest that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the yuan's recent gains against the dollar, says Mark Williams of Capital Economics . All the increase in the value of reserves are due to changes in exchange rates and market pricing, he says. "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  's recent inactivity is striking" as Beijing has rarely been quite so sanguine about sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves against the dollar in the past, he says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has probably become more subtle in managing exchange rates, trying to stay away from heavy-handed market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0540 ET - \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  's 2018 guidance--while seemingly in line with consensus--is disappointing upon further reflection because it implies "weaker underlying operating performance projections" than expected, Berenberg says. \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  expects 2018 core EPS growth of 2% to 5% at constant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a negative \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of 3% to 4%. This implies flat EPS growth this year, the bank says, which is "broadly in line with consensus." However, Berenberg says \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  that calculated \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact based on December, so the headwind is likely to be bigger because of the euro's subsequent strengthening. Furthermore, \uc2 Sanofi\uc2  's 2018 tax rate is lower than expected, and guidance already includes recent acquisitions, so the underlying situation may be weaker than it first appears, Berenberg says. (sonia.amaralrohter@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 07, 2018 08:56 ET (13:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180207ee270022q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
